Toys R Us plans to hire fewer emplary employees for the festive season
Toys R Us reports that it will not hire as many employees for the festive season as last year, at the same time the toy retailer for children claims that it will provide full-priority for full-time employees with the opportunity to work for more than an Hour.
The company reports that it plans to hire 40 000 people to work in stores and on wholesale bases throughout the country, which is less than those 45 000 that have been hired for the festive season of 2014.
The majority of jobs will be part-time jobs.
The company announced that it will start conducting interviews with the applicants this month and will increase the number of personnel from October to December.
Although there are still a few months before the holidays, the shopping season is getting closer, and companies are preparing to hire temporary employees in order to have enough state in stores and on the sale, shipment and delivery of goods.
Michael J. Fawke jokes about “dating” with Princess Diana
The premiere of the film “Back to the future” turned out to be a grandiose event for Michael J. Fawke.
It was noteworthy for personal reasons.
“We were sitting in the cinema and awaiting the arrival of the members of the royal family, I noticed that the place next to me is fluent, and then it dawned – Princess Diana will be sitting next to me,” he said in the trailer for the soon-released documentary “Just back in time”.
The film begins, and here it comes to my mind that I'm literally at arm's distance and in one false yon from a date with the princess of Welsh.
"Back in Time" - a documentary about "Back to the future" - includes an Interview with Fox, Leah Thompson and Christopher Lloyd, as well as director Robert Zemeckis and executive producer Steven Spielberg.
The premiere of the film “Back to the future” took place 30 years ago.
“For me,” Spielberg says, “it’s undeniably the greatest movie about time travel that has ever been filmed.”
"BACK in Time" will be available on VOD, a DVD and in some cinemas in October.
The head of the United Nations claims that there is not a military decision in Syria
Secretary-General Ban Ki-moon declares in response to Russia's military support for Syria that there is “not a military solution for nearly a quinquennial conflict,” and an increase in weapons will only exacerbate violence and suffering for millions of people.
The UN chief once again called on all participants, including the divided UN Security Council, to come together and support inclusive negotiations to find a political solution.
Ban Ki-moon said at a press conference on Wednesday that he is planning a meeting with the foreign ministers of the five permanent members of the council - the United States, Russia, China, the United Kingdom and France during the ministerial session of the General Assembly this month to discuss Syria.
He deplored that disagreements in the council, as well as among the Syrians and local authorities “have made the situation unresolvable.”
Ban called on the five permanent members to show the same solidarity and the unity that they demonstrated in resolving the issue of the nuclear program on Iran, and when considering the Syrian crisis.
The results of the survey, which shows that Donald Trump is not joking
