But a survey conducted by Monmouth University in early September reveals a hypothetical “one-to-one-on-to-one” antiquity competition between Trump and the majority of other Republican candidates, trump almost always receives the support of the majority.
He is ahead of Carly Fiorina by 13 points, Marco Rubio by 14 points, Walker by 15 points, Jeb Bourget by 19 points and finally Rand Paul, Jon Casich and Crisa Christie at 33 points.
He's got a nobody with Ted Cruz.
The only candidate who bypseuveres him?
Ben Carzon overtook the businessman by as much as 19 points in a hypothetical one-on-one competition.
Slightly more than one-half of supporters of Donald trump said that they have changed their mind.
