Assad called on all forces to unite in the fight against terrorism.
Syrian President Bashar al-Assad called on all forces to unite in the fight against Terrorism.
Assad is convinced that if Europe wants to cope with the problem of refugees, they must stop supporting terrorists in the Middle East.
The question is not that Europe accepts or does not accept refugees, but that it is necessary to eliminate the root causes of this problem.
If the Europeans are concerned about the fate of the refugees, let them stop supporting the terrorists.
This is our opinion on this issue.
“This is the essence of the refugee issue,” he said in an interview with RT.
We must continue the dialogue to reach a Consensus.
However, if we want real strides, it’s unpossible, as long as people are going to perish as long as they’re going through and people don’t feel completely safe.
“In this way, we are able to reach a consensus, but we can’t implement anything until we overcome terrorism in Syria,” Assad said.
