The pound sterling is growing as salaries rise in the United Kingdom
The pound grew against the background of rising wages in the United Kingdom, while the FTSE 100 index has risen thanks to the proposal to buy SABMiller.
From May to June earnings in the U.K, minus bonuses, increased by 2.9% compared with the same period last year.
The growth velocities proved the highest since 2009, and was greeted as a transfer to an earlier period of forecasts for a possible increase in quotations.
The escalated essatorium grew by more than 1% compared to the dollar and amounted to $ 1.5505 and 0.84% compared to the euro, amounting to € 1.3730.
FTSE 100 index grew to 6229.21 by 1.49%.
Against the general backdrop, SABMiller shares stood out, which grew by 20% thanks to the proposal to purchase received from AB InBev.
The deal would merge the world's two largest brewing companies, bringing together such brands as Budweiser, Stella Artois, Peroni and Golsch.
Burberry shares have risen by 0.9% against the backdrop of encouraging news from a competing group of luxury manufacturers Richemont.
Residual sales data for Richemont has surpassed all queeved expectations and showed that sales in a key market for Burberry began to rise again.
Glencore shares rose by 5% after the mining giant said it managed to receive $ 2.5 billion by placing shares, which was done as part of a strategy to reduce its debt.
Mondi's shares were the leaders in the fall in the indice - by 4.3% - after Goldman Sachs lowered the group's rating to "sell".
JD Sports shares grew after a sports clothing company reported an 83 percent increase in tax earnings for six-season six months to £46.6 million.
Chef of JD Sports says higher salaries may interfere with the Expansion
Peter Caugill, executive director of JD Sports, says that raising the minimum wage for British workers means “greater purchasing ability in the pockets of potential consumers”.
But it is unlikely that such purchasing power will outstrip the increase in the cost of labor costs, he says.
Expenditures may have influenced plans to expand JD Sports, he added, which could mean a decrease in additional vocabulance.
