Forecast is based on the assumption that Aldi next year will open 25 stores in the SA and $30 - in WA, achieving sales of $ 500 million and $ 600 million in these markets, respectively.
The loss of revenue and sales of food at a high level of constant costs of Metchash can cost the company about 13 million revenues before interest and taxes, said Mr. Kirat.
At the same time, Metcash loses market share in the eastern states, mainly due to Aldi and Coles, and this is the fact that a recent Morgan Survey found that IGA has the most loyal buyers.
McNal Stanley believes Metchash food sales will fall 3.8 per cent per cent in 2016, 4.1 percent in 2017 and 2.1 per cent in 2018, reducing the company’s market share from 14 per cent in 2015 to 10.3 per cent by 2020.
Hemisch Douglas, the founder of Magellan Financial Group last week, told Melbourne attendees that Metcash “may most likely to disappear within a decade.
Metcash refused to publicly comment on Mr. Douglas.
But it’s assumed that Metcash board member contacted Mr. Douglas last week.
IGA's market share has declined since 2010 from 18 to 14 per cent, and Metchash's revenues from the food business, which the company delivers to about 1,200 IGA retailers, have fallen by 43 per cent compared with 2012 due to operating leverage and due to a pressure on sales and profitability.
