And I think that Nick gained strength very quickly, which is proved by people like Federer and Murray, he grows in front of the public, he made a number of serious mistakes and deserves all the critique that he receives, but we are trying to help him to understand the consequences of his actions, and it’s necessary, I believe, I think, bring him out of the spotlight for some time so that he can think about them, and it’s best for the team for him.
The migration crisis in Europe: Hungary Announce an Emergencies, Closes the Border
Declaring the state of emergency, Hungary on Tuesday closed the border with Serbia on the southern border and detained those who are trying to infiltrate the country illegally to contain the flow of migrants flowing inside.
There were riots at the border - there were riots - hundreds of migrants accumulated on the border territory, to which the Serbian authorities reacted sharply negatively.
Stuck for an indistinctuated time on the section of the road between the checkpoints of the two countries, people who escaped armed violence in their homeland, smashed the tents and settled in this area.
Dissatisfaction was escalating.
When a police helicopter cirucked above them, the migrants shouted “Discover the border!” and shouted an insult to the Hungarian special police.
Some refused food and water in protest.
The Minister of Foreign Affairs of Serbia declared “unacceptable” the expulsion of migrants back from Hungary, when they come more and more of them from Macedonia and Greece.
“Sabre Serbia wants to be part of a solution to the problem, rather than colprint damage.
Negotiations are necessary in the coming days to hold negotiations with Brussels and other countries,” Ivica Dacic said in Prague.
Unemployment on the Hungarian-Serbian border began a day after a bloc of 28 countries was not able to develop a common immigrant policy at a joint meeting in Brussels.
The Ministers agreed to bear a common responsibility for the 40-kid 000 asylum seekers in overcrowded Italy and Greece and expressed the hope that an agreement will be reached next (next month or by the end of the year), according to which EU member states will accept another 120 000 refugees, including refugees from Hungary.
The German Chancellor Angela Merkel and Austria on Tuesday demanded to convene an external summit of the European Union next this week to discuss the immigration crisis engulfing the continent.
Hungary, however, does not look forward to hurried action from Brussels or its neighbors.
The state of emergency in the two southern regions announced on Tuesday gave the authorities more authority to act in relation to the crisis, which allowed them to block the roads and speed up court cases of asylum.
In the mean meantime, the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Hungary Peter Sziyarto said that his country also plans to harass the fence of barbed-wire on a part of the border with Romania in order to block the flow ofmigrants through the country, now that it has completed the fence on the Serbian border.
CBS News correspondent Charlie Dugata reported that even the inmates were connected to urgent work at the end of barbbitricated wiring fence between Hungary and Serbia.
Over the last few months, Hungary has become the main “nouflage place” and a border crossing point for Imigrations, many of whom are refugees – the victims of wars in Syria and the Middle East.
Nevertheless, the country's Prime Minister Viktor Orbán maintains the fact that the majority of people arriving in the country are economic migrants looking for a more prosperous life, and not refugees - victims of military actions who have the right to protection, and this point of view diverges sharply with the opinions of other EU countries, including Germany.
“The new laws, which came into force in Hungary at midnight, consider it a crime of crossing or damaging a 4-meter (13-foot) barbed-wire fence, built by the government along the southern border with the Serb area, and also include longer prison terms for those accused of traffic in human beings.
“Due to the situation caused by massive migration, the Hungarian government is declaring a state of emergency,” Zoltan Kovac, a government spokeswoman in the southern city of Seged, told report.
We make it very clear that an Illegal crossing of the border is a crime.
Formally, the parliament should still authorize the deployment of military forces, which is expected next week, but Associated Press reporters who are at the border have been observing the presence of armed troops with vehicles and dogs for several days.
Guergy Bakondi, Orbanov’s National Security Advisor, reported the capture of 45 people who were trying to cross the border at the very border, and another 15 people were inside the country.
They crossed the border, breaking the fence at the moment, are currently in police custody and are accused of committing administrative violations according to the new laws.
The authorities are quickly restoring the fence.
The Hungarian authorities on Tuesday in the morning also closed two of the seven aileas on the border with Serbia, driving to block one of the aisles a railway wag wag with barbed wrinkled wrinkled.
riots erupted on the main aisle across the border near the city of Ryoske (Hungary), since the Hungarians placed an office room to pass people inside a metal container, and crowds of people crushed each other to break through.
Approximately 20 people managed to get inside, while thousands of people stayed outside.
Another group of migrants blocked the main highway, leading from Serbia to Hungary, announced the abandonment of food and the water, until they are allowed to pass to Hungary.
