Veronik Laurie, the new CEO of Kingfisher, who owns a network of house-abrown services, said that behind this trend there is a significant influx of skilled craftsmen from Eastern Europe, offering services at minimum prices.
As a result, Kingfisher intends to open another 200 Screwfix stores specializing in convicts for craftsmen, and at the same time clapprote 60 B&Q stores.
Ms. Laurie said that she would like to see more women in the staff of B&Q stores, since eight out of ten decisions on purchases in the store are taken by representatives of the underfloor sex.
