Ms. Laurie said, “In our stores still work mostly by men.
Steps must be taken to achieve a Balancquest.
In general, half of our clients are women, and 80 per cent of decisions are made by women.
Women play an important role in decision-making.
Ms. Laury - one of the five women at the helm of leading British companies, whose shares are taken into account in the FTSE100 index, have also changed the composition of the top management team, achieving an equal number of men and women among directors.
Kingfisher - almost the only company in which exactly 50 percent of managers - a woman, including a general and a financial officer.
Ms. Laurie said: “This was a conscious decision, diversification is an important issue for us.
It was not difficult to find the right women on the board of directors.
