Kiev torravated the nuclear union.
Kiev has officially formalized the refusal of Ukraine to cooperate with Russia on the completion of Khmelnytsky nuclear power plant.
The Verkhovna Rada on Wednesday on the second attempt still voted for the dissolution of the agreement with Moscow.
Arrangements for the implementation of the third and fourth blocks were signed in 2010-2012, but it was not possible to start the implementation of the project.
On Wednesday, the Verkhovna Rada of Ukraine adopted a law terminating an agreement concluded in 2010-2012 with the Russian Federation on the construction of a third and fourth block at the Khmelnytsky nuclear power plant.
It was possible to carry out the bill submitted by the government of the country only from the second vote, for the first time it was supported by 210 deputies with the necessary minimum of 226, but then 234 members of parliament voted for the project.
Khmelnytsky NPP laid down under the USSR according to the initial project was supposed to have four power units of 1 GW with VVER reactors, but managed to build only two.
Negotiations with Moscow on the completion led to an intergovernmental agreement by 2010, in 2011-2012 the Verkhovna Rada adopted relevant laws.
Since there were no funds in the budget of Ukraine, it was assumed that it would have to build blocks on the loan of the Russian side, but the funds were never allocated.
After the coup in Kiev in February 2014 and the ensuing chewing in relations between the two countries, Kiev began to curtail relations with Moscow in the nuclear industry, announcing the refusal to cooperate on the Khmelnytsky Nutofan Nutopa feasibility study and a project to build a nuclear-fuel Fuel plant in Ukraine.
The only sphere where the relations have been preserved remained the purchase of fuel for existing Ukrainian nuclear power plants in the Russian Federation (provided about half of the generation of electricity in the country), as so far there has nothing to replace Russian deliveries.
From the plans for the completion of the Khmelnytsky nuclear power plant with a other contractor in Ukraine has not yet finally refused: back in 2014, in Kiev announced negotiations with the Czech Skoda JS.
The UN Secretary-General opposes the use of military force in the settlement of the Syrian conflict.
The Secretary-general of the United Nations Ban Ki-moon during a press conference said that it is impossible to regulate the situation in Syria by military means.
“There is no military solvary decision”, – quotes AP his response to a question regarding Russia’s military support of Syria.
Ban Ki-moon also said that he will hold a meeting with the foreign ministers of the permanent members of the UN Security Council on the situation in Syria.
I will hold a meeting with the foreign ministers of the UN Security Council member states later this month.
"There will be a meeting on Syria," he said.
Earlier today, Nikolai Bogdanovsky, the deputy head of the General Staff of the Armed Forces of the Armed Forces of Russia, said that the General Staff does not exclude the possibility of creating an air force base in Syria in the future.
So far there are no such plans.
“But anything can be,” said Bogdanovsky.
Earlier “Kommersant” reported that the United States does not trust the President of Russia Vladimir Putin, who said that military assistance to official Damascus is necessary to fight the terrorist group “Islamic state”.
To read in more detail about U.S. doubts about Russian assistance to Syria in Kommersant material, "The Russian Military Presence in Syria worries Washington."
In the OSCE PA reported on a possible meeting of parliamentarians of Ukraine and Russia.
The Chairman of the delegation of Ukraine to the Parliamentary Assemblegum of the OSCE (PA) Arthur Gerasimov said about the possibility of a bilateral meeting this year with Russian colleagues-parliamentaries to discuss the situation in the South-Invest-East of Ukraine.
“What I am aware of: a certain meeting is planned this year, perhaps between the Ukrainian and Russian parliamentary delegations,” Gerasimov said.
He also called for the implementation of the Minsk agreements and "to return to the normal functioning of our countries."
On the question of whether, in his opinion, it is currently possible a dialogue between Ukraine and Russia at the parliamentary level - in the Normandy format or in the format of a contact group at the site of the OSCE PA - Mr. Gerasimov noted that the dialogue was held, there are Minsk agreements.
At the same time, according to the politician, in Kiev supports any type of dialogue.
Earlier, the representative of Ukraine at the negotiations, ex-president Leonid Kuchma said that the self-proclaimed Donetsk and Luhansk republics did not fundamentally change their positions in the trilateral negotiations, but the tone of the dialogue has become more positive.
The parties were handed out their mandates.
Yesterday, the Nizhny Novgo Electoral Commission summed up the elections to the city Duma in the municipal district, distributing 12 deputy mandates played according to party lists.
Traditionally, a lot of complaints of violations during the elections sounded from representatives of the CPRF, accusing the electoral Commission of “covering falsifications”.
Opponent’s comments have not been accepted.
At the same time the election Commission refused the party “Communists of Russia” in the organization of a referendum on the abolition of fees for the overhaul of apartment buildings.
The city election Commission officially presented the results of the elections in the city Duma of Nizhny Novgorod in the municipal electoral constituency.
In total, 1.03 million people were included in the voting lists in Nizhny Novgorod, 746.7 thousand ballots were issued to the district commissions, and 268 thousand voters voted in the elections.
Invariably, more than 11.7 thousand bulletins were recognized as invalid, and more than 11.7 thousand ballots were invalidated.
Yesterday 12 mandates were distributed among political parties, depending on the votes they received.
On the lists of “Unified Russia” six deputy seats in the city Duma rely on Dmitry Svatkovsky, Dmitry Krasnov, Vasily Shupranov, Elizaveta Solonchenko, Vyacheslav Rasteryaev and Igor Nagorny.
The only LDPR mandate was received by party leader Vladimir Zhirinovsky.
The two mandates of the CPRF are distributed between Vladimir Bulanov and State Duma deputy Alexander Tarnaev.
Three mandates of “Fair Russia” goes to Alexander Razumovsky, Igor Bogdanov and Mikhail Shalyugin.
Now within five days these candidates have to decide whether they will work as deputies in the city Duma: in the event of a residue from the mandate, he proceeds to the next candidate for a party list.
The Chairman of the city election Commission Alexander Makeyev told the members of the Commission that he puts on duty to “sending telegrams Zhyirinovsky and others” for the purpose of abandoning mandates.
When approving the protocol on the results of the elections, CPRF representatives announced multiple violations.
Leonid Krasnokutsky, a member of the city election Commission with the right of deliberation from the CPRF Leonid Krasnokutsky proposed not to recognize the results of voting in the four constituencies No. 21-24, recalling that by the order of the head of the administration of the Sormovsky district, the entrance to the administration building, where four district commissions were located.
For a long time could not pass the deputies of the state Duma, nor the candidates themselves, nor the observers, and the resonant scandal with the storm of the doors of the regional administration was shown on television could not pass.
At the meetings of district commissions, all observers and members of commissions with the right of deliberative vote had an opportunity to be present.
The head ceased access to them only when the voting ended and the precinct commission did not yet come to hand over their bulletins.
This was done in order to prevent various provocations.
“Then the head was corrected, and at all the meetings interested persons could be present”, – retrieved Natalia Andryushina, a member of the city election commission.
The Communists objected that in the blocked building of the administration for more than four hours they illegally withheld the deputy of the regional assembly Lyudmila Aristova, about which a statement was sent to the Investigative Committee.
The opposition was also responsible that in a number of PECs on the day of the elections they began to seal the urns at 6-7 in the morning, laying out the ballots for early voting.
At the same time, there was no one not to notify the members of the commission with the right of deliberative votes and observers, so they came by the beginning of the elections at 8 a.m.
The communists are sure that in the morning before the opening of the polling polling stations in the urns could uncontrollably throw ballots.
However, the electoral Commission, which has already considered more than 124 complaints on various occasions, according to Alexander Makeyev, did not find any violations with stuffing unrecorded bulletins.
The members of the commission did not support the proposal of her colleague from “Fair Russia” Maria Popova through the regional election Commission to come out with amendments to the regional legislation in order to clearly establish the time for opening envelievates with ballots of early voting, which then fall into the urn.
“On the basis of your own initiative, please contact the CEC”, – advised Ms. Popova Aleksandar Makeyev.
At the end of the meeting with high-profile accusations, a CPRF member Sergei Samokhin, who shouted that the election Commission ignored dozens of complaints and covers falsification in the elections.
“You are not at a rally here, more carefully declare!” – offended the chairman of the election commission.
As a result, the protocol was approved almost unanimously.
Until September 27, the electoral Commission must approve the general results of the elections, after which within three weeks the first meeting of the city Duma of Nizhny Novgorod of the sixth convocation will be appointed.
In addition to decorating the results of the elections, the city’s election commission refused the political party “Communists of Russia” to register an initiative group for a local referendum.
Judging according to the documents, the party members were going to put two questions to discuss Nizhny Segodnitians: do they agree that fees for the overhaul of apartment buildings should “immediately be abolished”, and tariffs for housing and communal services “froze until 2020”.
However, the lawyer of the Duma Irina Maslova explained that the appeal “Communists of Russia” is contrary to the law.
FedEx Revenue has a mixed nature, a decrease in forecasts for 2016
FedEx reported the disappointing results of the last quarter, and the delivery service giant reduced the forecast for annual profit due to a drop in demand for cargo transportation services and an increase in costs in its land transport division.
Also, the company said that it plans to hire about 55 000 seasonal workers for the holidays.
At the Same time last year, FedEx announced that it will hire 50 000 temporary workers for the holidays.
Its shares fell by about 2.5 per cent in preliminary trading 45 minutes before the opening of the exchange on Wednesday.
FedEx Corp. said it plans to earn from $10.40 to $10.90 in the fiscal year, which ends next in May that it’s 20 cents less than in the previous prediction.
Analytiffs assumed $10.84 according to the FactSet review.
Declining the forecast is observed, regardless of an average increase of 4.9 per cent, which will come into force on January 4, and an increase in fees for ground transportation of heavy or assemblies, which begins in November.
The company said that it continues to plan an increase in revenue compared to last year due to reduced costs, increased gross revenues and an increase in online trading.
Chairman and CEO of Fred Smith said that the company “worked stably taking into account the faint, compared to the prognosis, economic conditions, especially in production and world trade.”
Plans to hire labor during the holidays were announced the day after the competitor’s statement, UPS, that they plan to hire an additional 95 000 Employees, about the same amount as they hired last year.
For the Quarter, which ended on Aug. on August 31, FedEx earned $ 62 million 6 per cent more than a year earlier.
Revenge per share amounted to 2.42 dollars, close to the forecast of an averaging 2.44 dollars per share conducted by Zacks Investment Research with a survey of 12 analysts.
Revenue increased by 5 per cent to $12.3 billion.
Six analysts interviewed by Zacks assumed $12.23 billion.
FedEx has been affected in recent years by a downturn in urgent international traffic, which led to a lack of increase in gross income in its express transportation unit.
However, the online shopping boom has sharply improved results in FedEx Ground.
Revenue from ground transportation increased by 29% in the last quarter, but operating revenues remained generally unreliable due to the increased costs of large-entry and self-sufficiency.
An express transport unit has received a higher income due to higher base rates, while in the freight sector the income has fallen due to an increase in labor costs.
In preliminary bidding about an hour before the opening of the exchange, FedEx shares fell by $ 3.85 or 2.5 per cent to $1.50.5.
They closed Tuesday, having fallen 11 per cent for a year and 17 percent lower than the June 11.
At the most-expected meeting in a few-thadio-flight, the heads of the Federal Reserve system will spend two days this week at a 27-foot table of Honduras mahogany, deciding if it’s time to raise the key interest rate for the first time in nearly a decade.
At one end, a richly declared meeting room with two-hundred-height two-floors, a wall image of the United States will hover over them.
This card is a reminder that the Chairman of the Federal Strategic system Janet L. Yellen and her colleagues should put the economic interests of the country above all others.
The Central Bank has received a double instruction from Congress: to increase employment in the United States as much as possible and keep stable prices here.
But since the Great Resistance, the leaders of the Federal system have recognized that there is a third unwritten instruction: financial stability.
And the third-guidance may prove to be an unfamiliar factor in an near-predicted decision on Thursday whether the U.S. economy is ready to break away from an unprincipled stimulus provided by an almost zero short-lived interest rate since the end of 2008.
Even though most of the data show steady economic growth, recent turmoil in global financial markets can hold already cautious executives of the Federal system from adding volatility by raising the base rate on federal funds - even by just a quarter of a percentage point.
“Obvious that the labor market and inflation will be the first and the most important subject of consideration,” said Lindsey M. Piegza, chief economist at Stifel Nicolaus & Co.
“However, I don’t think that if they were looking for a reason not to raise rates, the increased uncertainty around the global market is enough to give them an excuse to wait further,” she said.
There is no consensus about what will be done in the Federal reserve system, which in itself provokes fluctuations in the financial market.
Approximately half of economists recently interviewed by Bloomberg, predicted an increase in the interest rate this week.
Financial markets, however, are expecting that the Federal system will withstandraw from this, despite the fact that a key indicator shows only about a 30 per cent probability of a rapid rise.
This can lead to the fall of the stock market, if the federal system raises the bet, provided that those who take decisions do not soften the blow with a promise that the next increase will not soon.
On Tuesday, the Dove-Jones index rose 228.89 points, or by 1.4%, to 16 599.85.
The take-assembbell was provoked by the expectation that those who determine the strategy of the Federal system will leave a bet this week,” said John Lonski, chief economist at Moody’s Capital Markets Research.
“It will come as a surprise if the Federal system will raise rates at this point in time,” he said.
If the leadership of the Federal reserve system goes so, “they will have to go a long way in approving their strategy to keep financial markets in their hands so they don’t panic.”
Other experts objected that the rate hike could reassure financial markets, as this will remove uncertainty about how the Federal system will work.
JUST just a month ago, the Federal system seems to be leined to raise a rate of 0.25% this month, taking the first small stress to slower financial tightening, which could have confirmed the dynpality of U.S. recovery.
Yellen said in the spring and beginning of the summer that she was awaiting a rate hike this year, despite complaints from liberals that more economic progress was needed.
Although the emergence of new jobs slowed in August, the growth of the labor market was stable this year.
Unemployment has fallen to 5.1% last month, the lowest in more than seven years, and at almost the level that the federal system considers full employment.
Salary growth shows signs of acceloration.
And, although inflation continues to be lower than the central bank's annual figure of 2%, the leadership of the Federal system stated that a key reason was the temporary effect of a sharp drop in oil prices.
The economy “may cope with higher bets, and needs them, taking into account the reduction in the labor market,” said Ian Shefardson, Pantheon Macroeconomics chief economist.
However, financial markets around the world began shaking at the end of last month, after China devalued its currency.
The average Do-Jones stock index for industrial companies fell as much as 16% relative to a record-breaking value in May, as investors feared a slowdown in the Chinese economy could hamper global stunted global growth.
The market partially regained its position this month, and the Dow Jones index is now about 10 percent lower than high May.
For the leadership of the Federal reserve system indignation of the market additionally complicates the difficult calculating the timing of the increase in the interest rate.
“In the inaccessibility of what happened in the financial markets and the news about the weakness of the Chinese economy in the last few weeks, they would have twisted the nut at this meeting,” said Steven D. Oliner, a senior UCla Ziman Center researcher for the Real Estate and a former employee of the Federal Reserve.
Now, according to his forecasts, they will wait for at least a month to gain more control over the consequences.
“There’s a lot of unscrupulousness about the consequences for the U.S. economy, and there’s almost no reliable data since the latest developments in China,” Oliner said.
The health of the world economy does not fall within the main concerns of the Federal system, and it should technically not be taken into account when making these decisions.
But in essence, the Federal reserve system has become a global financial authority.
The influence of the Central Bank in recent years has been huge.
Only a hint from then-Truth Chairman Ben S. Bernanke in 2013 that the Federal Reserve could “molute” its monetary expansion has caused market turmoil around the world to turmoil.
In a world where markets and economies are increasingly intertwined with each other, it would be expected that the leaders of the Federal Standby system will not only monitor developments everywhere, but also consult with representatives of other Central banks and with experts in order to better understand the global economy.
Their decision-making is “rather an art than science,” said Zachari Carabell, head of Envestnet Inc, a company that deals with global wealth management strategies.
Geoffrey Lacker, president of the Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond, Virginia, noted this month that "the history of the Federal Warego system there have been instances of an overreaction to financial market movements, which do not seem to be unrelated to economic principles."
Lacker, a politician with the right to vote of an influencietal Federal Unveilable Committee, who insisted on a rate hike, cited 1998-99 decisions as an exemplary example.
The financial crisis in Asia led the Federal system to lower its base rate by 0.75% in three meetings “despite limited elusive consequences for U.S. growth,” Lacker said.
A year later, the leaders of the Federal system abolished these downwards.
“The federal reserve system should come first the concern for stability only in times of large crises, such as a market collapse in 2008, ”said Adam S. Posen, a former member of the interest rate setting committee at the Bank of England.
The last panic and did not come close to this level, he said.
“Of course, you wouldn’t want to end up in a situation where you are fascinated by rising bets because markets are shaking up,” Pozen, president of the Petersson World Economics, said.
“The Federal Standby System Act still has a double mandate and doesn’t mention financial stability, and until that changes, I don’t think they should be ahead of events.
