According to him, the President of Russia Vladimir Vladimir Putin “turned from a friend of the West into an enemy, the tsar, a dictator who suppresses the Russian opposition, who came to power undemocratically, despite the fact that he was elected as a result of democratic elections recognized in the West.”
Putin urged the international community to unite forces with Assad to the fight against the “Islamic state”.
commenting on the constant statements of the West that Assad himself should leave, he noted that the president comes to power with the consent of the people, through the elections, and if it leaves - then at the request of the people, and not according to the permission of the United States, the Security Council of the United Nations, the Geneva conference or the Geneva communiqué.
“If the people want them to stay – the president stays, and otherwise he should leave immediately,” he said.
Assad called Russia and Iran friendly countries and recalled that cooperation is being carried out with them.
