Lavrov and Kerry discussed the situation in Syria: Politics: World: Lenta.ru
US Secretary of state John Kerry held a telephone conversation with the Minister of foreign Affairs of Russia Sergey Lavrov.
About it reports Reuters with reference to the representative of the State Department John Kirby.
It is noted that the topic of the conversation was the conflict in Syria.
At the same time, Kirby did not provide additional details.
At the same time, he said that the United States has the tools to “further to isolate Russia”, if it supports Syrian President Bashar al-Assad, reports RIA Novosti.
As reported by the Russian foreign Ministry, Lavrov during a conversation with Kerry again stressed the need to create a united front to combat terrorist groups operating on the territory of this country.
We also discussed ways to resolve the Ukrainian crisis, possible steps to reduce tensions on the Korean Peninsula.
In addition, some issues of a bilateral nature were addressed.
Earlier, U.S. officials said that Russia is plundering its military presence in Syria and expressed concern about Moscow’s strengthening support for Assad.
