Eaten the victory for a couple of days.
World Athletics champion Sergei Shubenkov.
This season can be called a triumph for a 24-year-old athlete from Barnaul Sergey ShUBENKOV.
He managed at his corrugated distance of 110 merma hurriers to win at the team championship of Europe, to set several records, and most of the most important to become the world champion, the first in the history of the domestic barrier sprint.
In addition, recently the athlete won the final stage of the “Diamond League”, ranking in the overall standings the third place.
“Novye Izvestia” asked Shubenkov to share his impressions of the outgoing season.
Sergey, the season isn't over for you yet?
Yes, I am going to perform at the World Military Games, which will be held in October in Korea, and then I will think about the holiday.
However, now I will prepare at home, in Barnaul, and to be at home - it's still a completely different condition.
It’s more easy than hanging around the world every week.
Once you said that Autumn is a favorite time of the year for you.
At the end of August, the beginning of Sept. is a great time.
Spirties after the main start of the season lewed, the burden of responsibility does not put pressure.
You can compete for pleasure, on "relaxation".
Plus, you know that a vacation very soon.
Do you have any fatigue?
After all, the season is special, a lot of positive emotions ...
Fatigue by the end of the season always accumulate.
It doesn’t really matter what I’ve been doing, he’s winning or losing.
Each competition is stressful.
Constant flights, relocations - all this does not pass for the body with a trace.
Fatigue physically and emotionally.
Of course, my emotions are on the rise.
What's in there - I'm just happy!
By the time they finished at the World Cup in Beijing, do you come back often?
There's an opportunity.
Journalists don’t let me forget about it.
But in general, I believe that a bad athlete who lives with old victories scrolls his successful races again and again.
Eaten the victory of a couple of days - and you have to move on.
Preparing for this wonderful season was very much different from the accustomed?
I can’t say there was anything so special.
We began to get ready back in December, but I missed the winter competitive season.
Trained first at home in Barnaul, then at the training camp, then again at home.
It's all as usual.
But with the coach set the task: to try to get to a new level, at which I was not yet.
Almost all of the winter time was spent on laying the base.
Ran a pile of sneakers, performed exercises on general physical training, which included cravings and squat, and we pumped the back.
Then they began for barrier training, studied a lot of technology.
How did your rivals follow them?
I am always trying to do this, there is no problem in the Internet age.
Watched the winter championship of the European championship, and there in the barrier sprint the whole pedestal was occupied by the French!
Thought again: you need to do something, dilute this company.
With each start of this season, you have added and added results this season.
Did this give confidence?
I’ve been developing for the last few seasons about the same way.
There’s no such thing that I’m running at the first 13.20, and then 13.50.
I’m always reproducing my shape gradually.
The most important thing I wanted to do - to run out of 13 seconds.
All the work was aimed primarily at this result.
But the paradox is that you seem to feel that you are ready for feats, and at the competitions it does not always turn out to show their readiness.
How was it, for example, at the Olympics in the London Olympics?
I, to be honest, that semi-financial race (Shubenkov couldn’t qualify for the final. – “NI”) tried to forego right away.
Ready was very good, could really run out of 13 seconds.
Yes, even if he repeated his best result at that time, I would become the bronze medalist of the Games.
I'm unlucky.
Do you remember your first World Cup?
What's the matter?
It's happened in Tagu.
I really wanted to get into the final at that time at that time.
And faded right away from the turret, in the preliminary races.
Then I realized that rupture and greasing his head broke - it means you do not go anywhere at all.
After two years at the world Cup in Moscow has already reached the final with the best time.
I well remember my feelings before the decisive race: I really wanted to win “great gold” at that time!
How does it work, developing a decent velocity, do not also lose your head, do not turn off?
And this is the most difficult thing.
It is necessary to be very neat, focused on the technique, so as not to penetrate the barriers.
Noticed that when you tune in not for the result, but for the process is so much easier.
And the most high, when you have a feeling that you are fleeing and everything seems to work on its own!
Honestly, it’s worth it.
Many of our athletes from the outskirts after the first serious successes strive to move closer to the capital.
