Mithilitic clashes with the police took culmination on the border of Hungary.
Beigendacies staged protests on the border of Serbia, near the Hungarian village of Reske, which escalated into clashes with law enforcement.
As a result, the Hungarian police used water canopies and tear gas, reports Reuters.
Migrants throw the police with stones and trying to demolish the fence installed at the border.
Reinfor-reinforcements have been dispatched at the clashes, the police are taking measures in responding to aggressive actions by the migrants and their attempts to break the border.
According to Agence France-Presse, the refugees managed to break through the police cordon, after which dozens of migrants fled to the territory of Hungary.
Some of the refugees are evaporating from the Serbian-Hungarian border on the buses towards Belgrade and the border with Croatia, BBC reports.
The country's authorities have allowed migrants to arrive on the Croatian territory and ensure their transportation from there to the right country.
According to the authorities of Hungary, 20 police officers were injured.
On September 15, the Hungarian Parliament tightened the legislation on migration and border protection.
The amendments envisages the participation of the army in the protection of state borders, the criminal prosecution of those who illegally cross the border, as well as an expedited procedure for the consideration of asylum inquiries.
The Hungarian court has already declared one migrant guilty of illegally crossing the Hungarian-Serbian border, in connection with which it will be deported and will not be able to return to Hungary for one year.
In the near future, the Hungarian parliament also intends to consider the issue of the transfer to the armed forces of Hungary’s armed forces to protect the country’s parliament.
At the end of Judging, the authorities of Hungary began the construction of a fence with barbed wiet length of 175 km on the border with Serbia to curb the flow of migrants and refugees to the country.
The Russian confessed to committing the largest cyberattack in the history of the United States.
Accused of the largest cyberattack in the history of the U.S. Russian Vladimir Drinkman confessed to the the theft of more than 160 million credit card numbers, according to Reuters.
During the New-Jère federal trial, Drinkman confessed to conspiring to gain unsanitized access to computer systems and to commit scam.
During the meeting, the Russian spoke about collusion with three Russian citizens and a citizen of Ukraine, who are accused of cyberattack for 15 companies.
Aggregate damage was valued at $300 million.
“Respondents like Vladimir Drinkman, who have the skills to break into our computer networks pose a threat to our economic well-feasure, personal life and national security,” U.S. prosecutor Paul Fishman said in a statement.
Drinkman faces 30 years in prison, as well as a million-dollar fine.
When sentencing, the court will take into account the confessions of the Russian and, perhaps, will reduce his sentence.
Drinkman's verdict will be announced on January 15.
Vladimir Drinkman was arrested in the Netherlands in 2012.
At the same time, another suspect Dmitry Smilyanets was taken into custody.
The latter denies his guilt in the incriminated crimes.
Kerry warned Lavrov about the risk with Russia’s support of the Bashar al-Assad regime.
During a telephone conversation with the head of the Russian foreign Ministry Sergey Lavrov, US Secretary of State John Kerry warned that Russia’s support for Syrian President Bashar al-Assad exacerbates the conflict in the country.
“Secretke Kerry made it clear that Russia’s support for President Al-Assad risks exacerbating and enlarging the conflict, as well as jeopardizing our common goal to combat extremism if we don’t focus on finding a solution to the conflict in Syria through an effective political transfer of power.
Kerry has reaffirmed U.S.’s commitment to the Islamic State group (whose activities are banned by the Supreme Court) as part of a coalition of more than €60.
According to the Secretary of state, Assad "will never be able to be a reliable member" of the coalition.
Also in the course of the telephone conversation, Kerry stressed that the conflict in Syria can be resolved only through a political transition from Assad.
In the White house threatening Russia with isolation because of the support of the Assad regime.
On the eve of the press Secretary of the White house Joshua Earnest threatened Russia with isolation, if it does not stop supporting Assad.
As an alternative, Ernest proposed to join an international coalition that conducts an anti-terrorist operation against “Islamic state”.
In recent years, the media often reported the presence of Russian servicemen on the territory of Syria.
To which the head of the Russian foreign Ministry Sergey Lavrov said that Russian soldiers have been in Syria for many years and are helping the Syrians to develop equipment in order to use it against Islamists.
The four were killed when the police opened the shooting of rubber bullets on protesters in Nepal
Four people, including a 4-year-old boy, were killed in southern Nepal as police began firing with rubber bullets in a crowd protesting the country’s proposed new constitution, a spokeswoman said on Wednesday.
The violence took place on Tuesday evening in Ropandai County, about 175 miles west of Kathmandu, the capital.
Bishnu Prasad Dakal, the head of the district police, said that more than 1 000 protesters gathered at one of the police departments, some threw stones and incendiary bombs.
Mr Dakal said that the police used tear gas, then shot in the air before launching rubber bullets.
Twentieth members of the police and five civilians were injured, he said.
It is not clear why rubber bullets, which, as you know, can be killed, but they are traditionally used as a less lethargic alternative, caused such a high mortality.
This clamity was the last in a few weeks of bitter protests in the southern, flat part of Nepal, where Mademi representatives say that the new provinces formed under the new constitution will reduce their political influence.
Protests also took place in the west of Nepal, among Taru citizens who want to have their own state.
At least 40 persons, including eleven members of the police, have been killed in violent clashes, starting at 10.
Aug., when the four main political parties signed an agreement to divide the country into provinas, which was a decisive step towards a new constitution, but a very controversial issue in Nepal, which had been centrally administered for several centuries.
Work on the new constitution has been going on since 2008, but legislators have accelerated the process after a devastating earthquake that claimed the lives of thousands in April.
Legislators were voting for articles of the draft constitution in Kathmandu this week, and officials said that the new head will be signed by Sunday.
Sayyansk plans to create an enterprise for 900 jobs.
Sayyansk - the youngest city in the Irkutsk region.
Built in the 70-ies of the last century as the center of the chemical industry, has a developed infrastructure that requires systematic support.
A year ago Sayansk was headed by a new mayor - Oleg Borovsky.
About the results of the first year of work, about new projects and prospects, he told the correspondent of “Regular”.
Oleg Valerievich, why did you start working as a mayor?
First of all, I became acquainted with the results of audits of financial and economic activities, initiated an independent audit examination of the spending of local budget funds.
Then an audit of the municipal property was carried out.
One of the first practical steps was the reduction of document circulation to five days.
Previously, papers on instances could have walked for a month.
Measures were developed to increase the revenue base and optimize costs.
In November last year in Sayyansk held a visiting meeting of the government, which was considered the issues of socio-economic development of the territory.
In the city there did not have a design and estimate documentation (PSD) for a single object.
Without this, Sayyansk could not take part in federal programs.
We began with the preparation of PSD on the roads, a kindergarten, a northern sewage collector and a water conduit.
Now road works are already being carried out at two sites.
How is the decree of the President of the Russian Federation on the construction of children's ordains carried out in the city?
In July of this year 105 babies were born in Sayansk.
Such a positive demography in the city has not been observed for the last 27 years.
So the question of providing places in kindergartens today is one of the most pressing.
From September 1, closed for the overhaul of Kindergarten No. 10, designed for 320 places.
The estimated cost of the repair - 86 million ruble.
Such funds the city has never received such funds.
Last year after the refurbishment opened kindergarten number 23, which is now attended by 200 children.
Renovation was carried out on the terms of co-financing from the regional and local budgets, its cost amounted to more than 67 million rubles.
Thanks to the efforts of the administration and assistance of the regional government, funds were found for the purchase of furniture and equipment, the “People’s initiatives” program also helped.
There are plans to start the construction of a new Kindergarten in 2016.
With its introduction, we plan to eliminate the priority of children aged from one and a half to three years.
queuages for children from three to seven years old we do not have.
Investors have an interest in territory?
We have a clear understanding that construction in the city should be carried out, first of all, Sayan enterprises, it is they who need to be provided with a job.
Already in October is put into operation a 60-apartment house for orphans in the Leningradsky microdistrict.
As for the construction, I will add that Sayyansk is one of the four cities of the Angara region, which was included in the program for the construction of economy-class housing.
All necessary documentation has been prepared.
The construction of 90 block-secrets will begin in the near future.
In total, we announced the construction of 10 thousand square mortar of housing Writers to Participate in the program a lot.
One of the conditions - housing should be no more than 30 thousand rubles per square meter per square meter, this cost includes turnkey finishing.
If we cope with the specified volumes, we will continue to take part in the program.
As for investors, we also have other interesting projects.
At one time on the territory was built the Sayan Pig Complex, which in 2004 was sold for celestiality.
We are working with the Prosecutor’s office to challenge this transaction.
Moreover, the land under an object - in federal ownership.
Work is underway with Moscow, it is being decided to transfer 88 hectares to regional property, followed by the transfer of land to the municipality.
There is a potential investor, who is ready to invest 1.5 billion rubles in the reconstruction and the launch of the project.
With the launch of the pig complex we will have 900 jobs, which will be a great help for the city.
In Sayyansk developed the institution of social partnership?
Approximately 140 social and economic partnership agreements have been concluded.
A number of projects were carried out thanks to an active social position of business representatives.
Tangible support is provided by such enterprises as CJSC "Vostok-Center", Novo-Ziminskaya CHPP, OOO "Sayansky broiler", LLC "PC MDF", the management of these enterprises responds to all appeals.
Immediately by the Day of the city LLC "Sayansky broiler" gave the city a children's town, the company "Vostok-Center" renovated the sheated yard, where specialists deal with children with waste, expending more than 1 million rubble on it, spending more than 1 million rubles.
Thanks to the Spontaneous Means, it was possible to improve the territory of the city registry office.
Sponsors helped me colorfully celebrate City Day.
As in the old good days a paracet took place with the participation of urban teams and organizations.
The chronicle of the city was published, a book of Sayan poets.
Principled builders and people who have made a serious labor contribution to the development of Sayansk were awarded jubilee medals.
philanthropists also participate in the work of the City Charitable Charitable Foundation.
The very first step was the purchase of instruments for young talented musicians.
For nine months, more than 800 thousand rubles are aimed at supporting talented children to help children who are in need of expensive treatment, supporting children from low-income families.
How to solve personnel problems in the social sphere in Sayyansk?
In the city there is a shortage of doctors and pedagogical assistants.
To solve the personnel issue, it is of great importance for the provision of specialists with housing.
Over the last year, we have allocated five apartments for doctors, four teachers received official housing.
We have a program to allocate housing with the opportunity to privatize it in five years.
In the plans - the redevelopment of the building, which will be built another eight apartments for educators.
Also, teachers and doctors participate in the “Housing program for the Russian family”.
In the future - the construction of a house for employees of the public sector.
The most important thing is that in the city there is a workable team with which I can solve the most complex issues.
It’s important from all the crises to draw the right conclusions, and life does not dwell.
Potential for Sayansk and our region is great.
In the Duma introduced a draft law on the indexation of social pensions, taking into account the increase in prices.
The state Duma introduced a bill providing for the indexation of social pensions annually from February 1, taking into account the increase in prices.
The author of the document - the Deputy from "Fair Russia" Alexander Lomakin-Rumyantsev - also proposes an additional indexation of pensions on April 1, if the growth of the subsiditutive minimum exceeds the growth rate of prices for goods and services.
The indexation of social pensions, according to the current legislation, is carried out annually from April 1, taking into account the growth rate of the subsiditutive minimum of the pensioner in the Russian Federation over the past year.
The draft law, submitted to the lower house, provides for the introduction of the indexation of social pensions, taking into account the growth of consumer prices.
At the same time, carrying out the first indication is postponed to February 1, and the second is held on April 1.
The head of the PA of the OSCE said Mogherini about the inadmissibility of imposing sanctions against parliamentarians.
In an official letter to the High Representative of the European Union for Foreign Affairs Federica Mogherini, the speaker of the PA Ilkka Kanerva stated the inadmissibility of sanctions against legislators participating in the assembly events.
Nikolay Kovalev, a member of the Russian delegation told reporters about this at the autumn session of the OSCE PA in Ulaan-Batrop.
According to TASS reports, in support of Kanerva’s position, signed European parliamentarians, including the representatives of Germany, France, Italy, Cyprus and Greece.
"There has already been quite powerful support," Kovalev said.
Earlier, he said that the head of the PA of the OSCE came with the intention to collect the signatures of deputies, who pointed to the inadmissibility of imposing sanctions against parliamentarians.
In particular, Kovalev noted, Kanereva promised to raise this problem to the level of the leading structures of the European Union and “send an appropriate petition”.
