Flavors from Europe are at the risk of becoming homeless.
Only 23 St. Petersburg hotels have the right to accommodate tourists who in 2018 will come to see the World Cup.
Other hotels are in no hurried to obtain an appropriate permit.
According to the experts, this is a very disturbing sign.
On the eve of the world championship, the authorities will urgently have to come up with how to relocate all the guests of the city.
Interlocutors of “Rosbalt” believe that because of the tournament the cost of rented apartments will increase by 10-30%, and after the championship for removable dwelling will have to overpay.
The world Cup forced the authorities to pay attention to the state of Russian hotels.
According to the law, which is written specifically for the primacy, every hotel of St. Petersburg must undergo a classification procedure and prove that it corresponds to the stated number of stars and the level of service.
Already now it is understandable that it will not be possible for everyone to do this: hoteliers are so afraid of checks that they often do not even send documents to requests from the Federal Antimonopoly service in St. Petersburg.
Vadim Vladimirov told the head of UFAS, the department studied 138 hotels and now plans to start 34 cases against hotels, many of which simply did not respond to antimonopiuse workers.
There are signs that the management of three dozen companies deceived the citizens, placing a certain number of stars in an advertisement, said Vladimirov.
The problem is that now on account of literally each number, none can be lost before 2018.
Officials suspect that during the football championship the fans will occupy all the St. Petersburg hotels.
Now in the city of tourists can count on 30.5 thousand rooms.
According to Smolny, in St. St. Petersburg 17 five-star hotels, 51 four-star hotel, 100 - two- and three-star, 550 - one-star.
According to Nana Gvichia’s First Deputy Committee for the Development of Tourism, at the moment, only 23 hotels have been classified - so many inspections were carried out by companies accredited in St. St. St. St. Petersburg.
But whether any hotel ordered such a procedure from regional enterprises, Smolny is not known by an assimilate coincidence.
That is, there may also be a higher classification, but no one is aware of it.
“For the last six months, hotels did not really aspired to undergo a classification”, – admitted Ekaterina Shadskaya, Director of the North-Western Branch of the Russian Union of tourism industry.
This is due to the high season, during which the hoteliers earn the most money and do not want to engage in other things.
Another reason - the budgets in which the costs of verification were not laid, while the procedure can cost the hotel, depending on the status from 30 to 100 thousand rubles or more.
But still recently, the heads of hotels have become more active and began to apply for a classification, Shadskaya assured.
The hotels should have time before July 1, 2016, otherwise they will not only pay a fine, but will also not get the right to work at the world Cup.
It is already known that, according to the stalentness will be developed a fixed fee for a room in the hotel for the duration of the tournament.
The forms for which the cost will be calculated will be announced next year.
This is done in order not to allow the increase in prices by 200-300%, as it happens, for example, during the St. Petersburg economic forum.
It is necessary to have a conscience and do not allow an increase of two to three times, but the hotels need to be allowed to earn.
“I think the increase will be up to 50%”, – said the President of the Russian hotel Association Gennady Lamshin.
Vadim Vladimirov in turn is not sure that the fixation of prices corresponds to an understanding of the market economy.
I don’t know how much this fits into the framework of economic theory, but I hope that this measure is justified.
“It’s better than an unrestrained rise in price,” he said.
Unfamiliar what’s going to happen with popular cheap hostels.
Deputies of the state Duma introduced a bill according to which hostels should be banned in residential buildings.
We very much hope that this law will not be adopted or will not concern St. Petersburg.
“We will defend the point of view that the hostels should be preserved,” said Nana Gwachia.
However, according to her, the owners of mini-hotels in any case should be prepared to tighten the Housing Code.
If the state Duma still approves the bill, then in St. Petersburg will close about 80% of hostels, and at the moment there are 1.5 thousand numbers in them.
According to Leonid Garbar, the President of the Federation Restaurateur and Hoteliers of the North-WaspCT Leonid Garbar, in St. Petersburg there is a lack of two and three-star hotels, which are just in demand by football fans, but there is a skew against hotels with four and five stars.
Such a state of affairs is similar in the same situation, when there are 75 thousand VIPs at the 80-thousand Stadium.
This can be corrected at the expense of mini-hotels.
Their possible ban, the expert considers “idolicism”: “It seems to me strange that some people can live in apartments, but for some reason visitors can’t.”
If the hostel is a dormitory, I don’t agree that it’s wrong.
But if it's like the hotel in which guests come in for a short period of time, why don't you?
Mini-hostels risk skipping the World Cup and because of their lack of gratification.
Hundreds of small hotels simply won’t have time to pass the classification, and the yam is dug for themselves.
By the summer of 2016 the works will be booked by all hotels of the city.
“Compancies, which can carry out this procedure are not so much, so they will abandon less paid orders from mini-hotels, and will choose those that are more expensive,” said Gennady Lamshin, adding that in a number of cities, for example, Moscow and Volgograd, the indicators of checks passed at the moment are much higher than St. Petersburg.
The reason for the St. Petersburg delay lies, among other things, with constant reshuffles in the tourist block of the government, which does not contribute to well-coordinated work.
According to the experts, if there is not enough for St. Petersburg hotels for everyone, which is most likely to have to pay attention to regional hotels and holiday homes.
According to the example of celebrating the 300-anniversary of St. St. Petersburg in the city can mobilize the river fleet, that is, the guests of the tournament will be able to live in shelters.
In addition, many of the fans will be prepared on the vans, in which it will be possible to spend the night.
“The main thing is not to tune so many hotels so that later they are empty,” Gennady Lamshin said.
Also very popular during the football championship will use removable dwelling.
