"It's Impossible for everyone to come to Europe" - Dalai-Lam - RT
“Europe can’t accept all refugees, the Dalai Lama said, adding that a real solution to the current refugee crisis lies in the Middle East.
The leader of the Tibetan Buddhists called for an end to the violence in countries that are the homeland of refugees.
The Dalai Lama touched upon the ongoing refugee crisis in its speech at the opening of the Dalai Lama Compression Center in Oxford on ethics research at the beginning of its 10-day visit to the United Kingdom.
He stated that in the existing circumstances the interests of mankind should be higher than the interests of individual countries or even continents.
He also stressed that, although this is admirable, the reaction of Western European countries to the refugee crisis is inaccessible.
“It’s impossible for everyone to come to Europe,” he said in a speech.
Although the Dalai Lama spoke highly about the actions taken by Germany and Austria in connection with the crisis, he stressed that this is only a temporary solution.
Worries about thousands of refugees is great, but at the same time you have to think about durable solutions, how to bring real peace and real development, mainly through education, to these Muslim countries,” he said.
At the end of an end, we need to think about how to reduce homicides in their countries.
We need to weaken the use of force.
The use of force has never solved these problems,” he added.
Responding to the violence, the Dalai Lama also commented on the actions of George H.W. Bush after 9/11 terrorist attacks, stating that U.S. harsh reaction launched a chain of uncontrollable events.
After 9/11, my congratulgence I expressed my congratulations in a letter to President Bush and I told him that a solution to this problem was possible through non-violence.
I am aware that his intentions were good, but he used force, and this has caused unexpected consequences, ”said Dalai-Lama.
Quarterly increase in the number of children who have swallowed a disinfectant for hands, over the last 4 years
Toxicological centers in the U.S. reported an almost 400 percent increase since 2010, the number of children under the age of 12 who have swallowed arm disinfectants with a high-yielding alcohol, according to the toxicological center of the state of Georgia.
Doctor Gayord López, director director of the Georgia State Tusocial Center, cases of stalking children under the age of 12 hand disinfectant fluids reported in toxicological centers increased from 3266 in 2010 to 1,6117 in 2014.
“Children come into contact with these substances more often, and, sadly, a certain percentage goes to an ambulance station,” Lopez told CNN.
He said that some children drink dissincretizing liquid specifically, and some do so to impress their friends, or a dispute for social networks.
In videos on Youtube you can see teenagers drank dissincrigting as a cheap booze.
teenagers reportedly bleed the disinfectant fluid with the alcohol-containing germination fluid to get a stronger drink.
Children of younger age can attract pleasant sanctuary sanctifying fluid.
“The child doesn’t think this can hurt him,” Lopez said.
Many of the most attractive (disinsipating hand liquids) - those that are aromatized.
There are disinfectants for hands with the smell of strawberries, grapes, an orange, which are very attractive for children.
The disinfectant for the hands contains somewhere from 45 to 95 percent alcohol.
In young children, in particular, only a few sprays can cause alcohol poisoning.
“It’s high-continued alcohol,” Dr. Stephen Tønton, chief medical officer at Kansas at the University of Kansas Hospital, told Fox 4 in Kansas.
You wouldn’t just leave a glass of whiskey like that, but the people keep these disinfectants for your hands, and if the children reach them, it’s a quick way to use a large amount of alcohol.
Naija Russell, a six-year-old girl who recently swallowed arm disinfectant with strawberry fragrance in the amount of about four spray, was sent for treatment to the ambulance.
The level of alcohol in the blood she had 179, twice as much as that of an adult, who by the law is considered in a state of alcoholic intoxication, according to Dr-Kris Ritchie - an ambulance doctor who healed her at Gwinnet medical center near Atlanta.
Naija confiscated words and couldn’t walk when she was taken to an ambulance.
Physicians observed her all night in a separate pediatric clinic in order not to miss any signs of a cerebral injury, because because of alcohol, the girl fell and hit her head, Ritchie said.
"It was very terracticable," Ortoria Scott, Naiji's mother, told CNN.
It could have been deadly for my child.
López recommended that parents and teachers use non-a-al-propaganda or disinfecting napkin, in addition to removing disinfectant fluids for their hands from children's reach zone.
In addition to alcoholic poisoning, some disinfectants are associated with deaths.
In 2013, two Ontario women died after swallowing a sanctuary containing a toxic undeclared ingredient.
Health officials suspect the product contained methanol - a lethal agent, not ethyl alcohol, which was indicated as an active substance.
In January, a fourth-pril student in northern New York conspired conspired to poison their “nasty” teacher by “distributing antibacterial substances in the classroom,” according to a police report.
The teacher has a strong allergy to hand disinfectants, and she forbade keeping them in her own class.
The police believe that the unsuccessful plan was “empty conversations”, and addresses the issues of disciplinary discipline for the school district.
As the oldest children's library in Barnaul became a family club.
On the bezel's beser at the entrance to the regional children's library named after N.K. Krupskaya groves a cast-iron owl.
Kids, who come for the books, try to feed her with candy.
For several generations he has been going to this library for 95 years.
The most first readers in the twenties of the last century staged loud readers here, staged performances according to Mayakovsky's rumors, conducted literary quizzes and corresponded with Lenin's wife.
Correspondence lasted for four years, and, as the "Junior Steel" newspaper wrote in 1939, every day "the friendship between Nadezhda Konstantinovna Krupskaya and the friends of the children's library of Barnaul" became stronger.
Nadezhda Konstantinovna even once exiled her children's photo to distant Barnaul friends.
And when Barnaul residents were asked whether Nadezhda Konstantovna objected that the library should be assigned her name, she wrote that she did not mind.
Writing has long been trampled in the museum, and the grandchildren and great-great-grandchildren of the first readers have to explain whose harsh profile is decorating the bas-relief on the library building.
During perestroeterration, various people often called, resutilated: why the children's library does not be renamed?
Let there be a library of the name of some good children's writer, without a political color!
Employees of the library sat down, thought, and decided to leave everything as it is.
"Krupskaya" - this is, perhaps, the most well-known and favorite library in Barnaul, like "Leninka" in Moscow.
On the floor in the biliary lounge is a yellow-brick track.
"Wizard of the Emerald City" - the favorite theme of the artist Oli Moskovka.
Previously, Olya was a manager in a law firm, came to work at the age of eight, went into five, and from all the other managers differed only the love of drawing.
And then I found an ad on the Internet: "We need an illustrator for a book."
The book was written by a small American girl, and she was called "My Cancer Mommy".
Olya made illustrations, and thought: life can end at any moment, and there will be no miracles in it if you do not create them for yourself.
Now she works in the library, Illustrates children's books of writers around the world and compose fairy-tale fairy-tale.
It is traditionally believed that the children lose interest in the book that they are increasingly living in some kind of virtual space.
But reading children come to us, and their parents understand the meaning of the reading, ”said Tatyana Kushwid, director of the library.
In the last years, we even have such a moment of confidence that a children's library is needed, and it will live - the children come here!
It seems to me that the interest in reading is coming back.
In the lounge of the library hangs a large exhibition stained glass window with an updated photo exposition.
Once in the quarter hang new photos of readers who go to the library with the whole family: mother, father and children.
The library rejoices that their fathers began to come with children more and more often.
If at the age of two the child was read only Chukovsky, at an older age he needs books more difficult.
But now there is a law according to which an eight-year-on-year-old prodigy is forbidden to issue books out of category 12+.
To receive such a book, the child must bring their parents with them - they come, then they return again, and gradually "Krupskaya" becomes for them something like a family club.
In the library there are Treasure - a pre-revolutionary collection of epics and spectators, Korolenko's story in an appendix to the magazine "Niva", the moustard "Murzilki" for 1936.
After all, now we are now not only the conceptual space of the “chram of the book”, we are now open to the movement, we are trying to become a special place: not a house, not a job, not a school, ”explains Tatiana Kushvid.
You can come to us to re-read, play, draw.
We made a game zone for the toddles - the child just comes to play, and the hand still reaches for the book!
Some of our readers their parents carry away, and they stop with their legs, they do not want to leave.
Often mothers with wheelchairs come - and we are pleased that they put the library in the first place among all the other places to come with the kids.
Tatyana Kushvid says: modern children, just like we once love classical children's literature:
Publishing is now developing, and a lot of attention is paid to the authors, who are a link between generations.”
And if we talk about young children, then it is important for them to be a hero who travels from one book to the other.
Kids don’t like to part with their heroes.
The library constantly releasing booklets for parents, in which it tells what is happening in modern children's literature, what books it is necessary to pay attention to and why.
Buklets are so fascinating and intriguing that adults are also interested, but this library is still not for them.
Remove books outside the reading room for adults is prohibited.
This magical privilege is found only in the children.
In the most distant room of the library there is a square hatch with an ancient wooden staircase in the basement, in a book depository.
Feces will be whiggled under your steps - this is a very old machine of time.
With the book of your childhood, you meet like an old comrade: hello, it is good that you and I don't change.
Ellie still cheerfully walks on the road, paved with a yellow-brick, the laundress of Tol Ryzhikov steals magical matches, and the Kibalchis boys did not tell the Dictated Bourgeois of Military Mystery - he already has a firm word.
Such books - as passwords, you can find out on them any place of your own.
There are in the repository and there are real book rhinestones - for example, a pre-revolutionary collection of epics and heroes.
Or Korolenko in the famous appendix to the magazine "Niva".
Or "Murzilki" for 1936.
The time has put the pages old, painted them into a tea color.
These publications are no longer given to readers.
These are shards of our future collection, I all dream - I will re-retire and deal with rare children's children's books.
But the children for this, so so to speak, will not lead: the colors in the old books are not very vibbitory, and the themes ... you open the first page, and there - Lenin, party, Komsomol.
Now it seems: why did we all prescribe this "Pioneer's truth?"
But still it was interesting, - Galina Ilyasova tells the "Earring Planet", the head of a book depository.
"Murzilki" pages darkened from time to time.
Galina Vasilyevna manages a book repository throughout his life.
She knows the color of Buratino’s wizard, in what academic year Harry Potter became the captain of Griffindor’s team at the Quiddic championship, in what situations Carlson uses the silencer for the motor, and by whom Alice Selezneva’s father works.
For the work of the librarian pay little, and everyone who can live without these book rows very quickly finds a different profession very quickly.
There remain only the most Continued: educators, educators, ministers of the cult of the book.
They you can also find out by a smush - it is believed that this is a professional trait of a children's librarian.
If he smiling at the first minute of a conversation - it is a professional.
In general, I love children's books: as a librarian I like, so that they should stand smoothly and beautiful on the shelves, and I also adore to read them, - says Galina Vasilyevna.
I am reading everything: military, historical stories, fairy tales, fiction.
I read modern Russian writers, fresh translations ...
Of course, it seems to me that in my childhood everything was different.
The books were the funniest and most exciting of what was going on with me at that time.
And so since I was insanely fond of them, it seemed to me that the library is a magical place.
And I wanted to work where everyone is sitting and reading.
I'm hoping there will always be books in spite of pediatricians.
And I rejoice, when our ex-readers bring their children, and even grandparents.
