Unemployment among Scots does not change, while in the United Kingdom as a whole it is growing
UnEQUIBILITAT IN SECHOdried 164 000 people between May and J.July, while the number of unemployed in the United Kingdom as a whole increased by 10 000 to 1.82 million.
Unemployment rate in Scotland, 5.9%, was higher than the United Kingdom at 5.5%, according to National Statistics (ONS).
At the same time, employment in Scotland fell by 12 000 people in a three-propagian, while the number of employees is now 2 612 000.
Unemployment for Scotland dropped to 74.0 per cent in a quarter, an average of 73.5% in the United Kingdom.
The Minister of Affairs of Scotland David Mandell, commenting on the most recent figures, noted: “The long-term plan of the government has laid the basis for strengthening the economy.”
It’s been almost exactly one year since Scotland made a historic decision to remain part of the United Kingdom.
During these 12 months, we have seen a further improvement in Scotland’s labor market with rising employment and reducing unemployment.
