FriendSFest: a comedial show that has taught us serious lessons of male friendship
The absence of such stories catches the eye, especially when you consider how precarious the need of men for frankness has become, now more than ever, despite the fact that the suicide rate among young men is at a maximum for 15 years.
In 2013, this was the single largest cause of death of men between the ages of 20 and 45 in the United Kingdom, three times as likely to occur with men than with women.
In an attempt to deal with the “Campaine Against Unhappy Lives” has declared 2015 the Year of the Men to challenge a culture that doesn’t allow men to come for help when they need it.
Friendship is at the center of this battle to take this challenge.
A recently conducted study of more than 2 000 students of universities who show symptoms of depression found that if the patient has a sufficiently large number of friends "in a normal mood", the chances of a cure are doubled.
Equally, for those who are out of depression, the circle of mentally healthy friends havoces havoces halve the chance of mental disorders.
But, of course, for the friendship to work, first of all, it is necessary to have it.
In an era when communication is managed by social networks, when the styre prefers to content, the speed of the answer is often valued more than a meaningful contact.
Our digital life is doubling the need to seem strong, loving with fun and successful, even if loneliness reigns in reality.
Such superficial success depends on the fact that psychologists call external values - money, the image, social status, completely at the expense of internal values, our internal desire for personal growth and friendship, which has a stronger effect on our mental health.
And, as one billionaire recently retaliated, the creator of a video game, for the money you really do not buy any more happiness.
Disadvantages of Friends is that they draw attention to it.
Each of the Characters Was Determined not through his work, but, rather, through a personality that manifested itself in communication with his friends.
Joey Humor and Chandler’s constant hug, moments of viewing football on comfortable stools, swirls in Rachel - everything proceeds from the understanding that men can feel it, even if they often refrain from fully studying their feelings.
According to Samaritation, an employee: “My role as a listener for people who feel depression and suicidal sentiment emphasizes how even the smallest communication of friends can bring benefits.”
Often those men who come to us feel incapacitated with friends.
“Lie live with it,” as well as the feeling blasphemous conversation about problems can be perceived as a weakness.
Friends is one of those shows that comes to my mind when I’m trying to offer arbrupt collating mechanisms.
It emphasized the unobtrusive moments of male friendship.
As it is concerned about my task, the status of an out-of-compartment, talking on the phone helps people in moments of desperation, long-term support comes from the inner circle of family and friends.
