Di-Paradia scores a goal, helping PSG to smash “Malmo”
Ánel di-Maria on a par with Blaise Matyudi and Edinson Cavani celebrating the goals scored against Malmö.
Angel di Maria, debuting in the Champions League, scored a goal, which allowed PSG to easily beat Malmö on Tuesday.
Here's the match report and the reaction to the game.
Angel Di Maria and Edinson Cavani did their job when Paris Saint-Gérène started playing in the Champions League with an extremely convenient 2:0 against Malmø at the Park de Prennes Stadium on Tuesday.
Di Maria scored the ball less than in four minutes after his first game in the Champions League began as a PSG player to set a referral to the champions of France, but they missed a number of opportunities before they finally increased their advantage when Cavani scored the goal in the 61 th minute.
Along with "Real Madrid" and Shakhtar Donetsk in group A, "Paris" had to take a good start in the game against the champions of Sweden, because they were aimed not at qualifying the play-off, but at the continuation of a series of successful games of the last three seasons, where they reached the quarterfinals.
They earned points, but at the same time it was not the best decision from Laurent Blanc to consider Zlatan Ibrahimovic as useless in the ass and later to replace him on the pitch in a game against a team from his hometown and the club, in which he began his brilliant career in 1999.
"It's not easy - to win at home at home or on a party in the Champions League, so it's like to win with a score of 2:0, to give the opponents the problems and to play a great defense - it's a good start, even if there are still moments that we will need to finalize during the season," Blan said.
It's a promising thing.
We wanted to win, and we didn’t, even though I pity we didn’t hit one or two goals bigger.
Ibrahimovic returned after an injury in one of the substitutions as part of the Paris team, which brought her a draw with a score of 2:2 against Bordeaux in the first league over the weekend, but he was pushed back to Di Maria in the fourth minute.
An Argentine striker was spotted as a player able to bring PSG to a new level in Europe, after he was bought from Manchester United last month, and he proved why, when he ran away from Marco Verratti behind Malmö’s defense and beautifully completed an attack, sending the ball past Johan Willand into the far corner of the goal.
However, if someone then was expecting an easy-and-givoy from PSG, they had to be frustrated.
“Malmø”, who defeated Celtic in the playoffs to get to this stage, having nine world-class players on the field at the beginning of the game, five defenders and two defensive midfielders in the middle of the field was a serious opponent.
But, with the exception of Nikola Djurzic's strike, in which the ball flew past Kevin Trapp's backstroke at the 34 th minute, they attacked quite a bit.
But PSG at some times supplied itself with uncompensatory passes and weak attacks, especially from Ibrahimovic, which only in the first half could not realize at least five attempts, and then could not process the ball scored by Cavani immediately after the resumption of the game.
Nevertheless, he showed himself to be much more skillful in precise passes, and it was a pass from Ibrahimovic, having received which, Di-Viae sent the ball with a swollen punch, which went to the rod by Villanda at 52 minutes.
The second goal was finally scored after an hour-to-minute note thanks to Cavani, the Uruguayan scored his sixth goal in the season after Ibrahimovic coranced the ball, sent to the center of the field from Maxwell's left flank.
This puts an end to any of the ideas that Malmö had regarding the return to the game, and only Willand's interception at a close distance did not allow David Luis to increase the final score before Esecaille Lavessi, who came out to be replaced, did not count a goal at the very end of the match.
Málme coach Age Hareide later admitted that PSG was a class higher than his team, while the Norwegian said: "Our last game in the Champions League took place in December last year."
Since then, we’ve only only played in the Swedish league, and that’s not that level.
Qualifying isn't enough.
Glory "Paris"!
It’s a lovely game with them.
Glencore Earning $2.5 Billion
Located in Switzerland mining and commercial giant Glencore, affected by the decline in commodity prices, earned $ 2.5 billion on the sale of shares as part as part of its ambitious plan to reduce the debt.
Glencore quoted on the London Stock Stock Exchange made a statement that he has traded new shares in the amount of about 1.6 billion pound sterling in order to repay the debt.
The company, which has lost 57 percent of its market value, is trying to cope with the collapse of commodity prices, while China’s economic decline is derebating demand and wretched, creating chaos in global markets.
Thanks to the issuance of new shares at a preferential price, Glencore shares on the London Stock Exchange soared in early morning trading on Wednesday.
The shares jumped 2.77 percent to 1,31.60 pence on FTSE 100 index, which when opened trading 0.69 percent higher.
Glencore last week began selling $2.5 Billion in vast plans to cut its 30-billion-debt-debt by about a third.
The company sold new promotions for 125 cents apiece, that is, with a discount of 2.4 percent to the price at the close of trading on Tuesday.
It placed 1.3 billion new shares, which is 9.99 percent of the authorized capital of the company.
Due to fears about the continuation of the decline in the Chinese economy, iron ore value decreased by about half, while charcoal, copper and other raw materials fell in price by 20-40 percent.
The White house confirms Xi Jinping’s visit to Washington
The White House confirmed in an official statement Tuesday that Chinese President Xi Jinping will pay an official visit to the U.S. at the end of this month.
This visit – Xi Qinpin’s first visit to D.S.D. – will take place on September 25 and will receive a return visit to President Barack Obama’s arrival in Beijing in November last year, the statement said.
U.S. President and First-Laides Michelle-Obpochelle Obama will also accept Xi Jinping with Peng Liyuan's wife at a government dinner this evening after the two leaders hold bilateral talks.
President Xi Jinping's visit will provide an opportunity to expand U.S.-China cooperation on common, regional and bilateral issues of interest to both sides, as well as allowing U.S.-China presidents to constructively address the controversial themes."
It is expected that XI Jinping, whose visit was first announced in February, will stop in Seattle to meet the leaders of several leading American technology companies on their way to Washington, and then go to New York to participate in the September UN General Assembly.
It is expected that Obama and Xi Jingpin will discuss a number of controversial issues, including Washington’s concerns associated with alleged cyber espionage from China and the growing categoricalness of China on the issue of the controversial South China Sea.
Shot down the biker at Kutuzovsky Lachech received 2 years of colony.
In addition, the court partially satisfied the civil actions of the victims against Denis Mirzoev in the amount of 1.2 million rubles.
Dorogomilovsky court of Moscow sentenced Denis Mirzoev, who killed a motorcyclist on Kutuzovsky Prospekt in Moscow.
Mirzoev received a sentence of two years of incarcerated imprisonment in a penitentiary-settlement.
He was found guilty under the article “Violation of the rules of the road and the operation of vehicles” of the Criminal Code of the Russian Federation.
In addition, the court partially satisfied the civil claims of the victims in the amount of 1.2 million rubles.
In the course of the deliberations of the parties, the prosecutor asked Mirzoev to three years in prison and to recover from him the claims of the victims in a proper amount - eight million rubles.
The accident, which is in question, occurred on May 22 at about three o'clock in the morning in the area of the house of the house of Kutuzovsky Prospekt.
The BMW car, at the wheel of which Mirzoev was located, crossed the oncoming lane and hit a motorcyclist standing on the side of the road.
From the received injuries a man born in 1989 died on the spot.
The friends of the deceased in social networks reported that the driver of the BMW was driving at great speed and before the accident went to the oncoming lane.
Fearing that the driver will try to evade responsibility, the bikers staged a motor rally from Vorobyov mountains to the GUMVD of the Federal Internal Affairs of Moscow on Petrovka.
Soon after, it became known that the investigation after the interrogation detained the alleged culprit of the accident.
In Moscow detained a naked man coming to the temple.
He behaved quietly and did not commit any illegal actions, the police handed it to the doctors of urgent psychiatric care.
Employees of the Metropolitan police detained a resident of Moscow, who went to one of the churches without clothes.
This is reported by the Agency “Moscow”.
As the head of the press service of the Ministry of internal Affairs in Moscow Andrey Galikaberov said, the incident occurred on Tuesday, September 15, at about 16.00, on the Kashirskoye highway.
A naked man entered the church of St. Nicholas.
He behaved quietly and did not commit any illegal actions.
An outskirts of the police arrived.
Law enforcers were awaiting doctors from an emergency psychiatric brigade and handed them a man.
It turned out to be a 26-year-old resident of Moscow.
Vladimir Yakushev signed more than 40 resolutions and orders.
More than 40 resolutions and orders were signed by the Governor of the Tyumen region Vladimir Yakushev at a meeting of the Presidium of the regional government.
Part of them concerned the allocation of funds for educational and medical institutions in the municipalities of the region.
In particular, funds were allocated for the purchase of a bus for one of the schools of the Nizhnetavdinsky district for the overhaul of the regional hospital in the Kazan district.
As stated in the accompanying documents, the money will go to the completion of the overhaul of the second-floor of the therapeutic department.
There will be arranging networks of hot and cold water supply, drainage, power grids and electrical equipment, ventilating systems, the facade of the building will be put in order in order, renovated the premises, carry out a set of measures for fire safety and energy saving will be carried out.
In Sochi, there will be a second forum of the regions of Russia and Belarus.
On September 17-18, the second forum of the regions of Russia and Belarus will be held in Sochi, in which the Tyumen delegation headed by the governor will take part.
About the upcoming event in Sochi and the interim results of the cooperation says the honorary consul General of the Republic of Belarus in Tyumen Vladimir Shuglia, who was part of the official delegation.
Vladimir Fedorovich, what tasks does the Sochinsky forum set?
A large-scale event in Sochi reflects the industrial policy of the Union State.
It is built on the fruitful cooperation of the regions - important ties of relations between the two states.
It is planned to be attended by the President of Russia Vladimir Putin and the President of the Republic of Belarus Oleksandr Lukashenko.
In the framework of plenary and sectional meetings we will talk about the experience of the regional and local authorities of Russia and Belarus in the implementation of the industrial policy, the regulatory and legal support programs of the Union State.
At the forum will be addressed by the Governor of the Tyumen region.
I think that this testifies to successful, sustainable inter-regional interregional cooperation between the region and Belarus.
Representatives of relevant ministries and departments, Russian and Belarusian entrepreneurs will also arrive at the forum.
There will be trade fairs and specialized exhibitions, including from the Tyumen region.
I hope that the forum will help to conclude new lucrative contracts and agreements.
I will add that the first such meeting took place in Minsk in June last year.
Its work was attended by more than two hundred delegates, including 19 regions of Russia.
At the same time a very important cooperation agreement was signed between the Tyumen and Minsk regions.
About the significance of our developments is evidenced by the fact that in Tyumen there was a meeting of a permanent seminar at the parliamentary meeting of the Union of Russia and Belarus.
In addition, the delegation of the agro-industrial complex of the Tyumen region has visited the Republic of Belarus in order to study the work of Belarusians in the preparation of personnel for agriculture, to identify additional points of contact and the organization of new investment projects in the agro-industry complex.
Recently you have met the head of the region and the head of the city administration.
What topics were discussed?
During the meeting with the Governor of the Tyumen region, Vladimir Yakushev, we were talking about regional cooperation with the Republic of Belarus in these difficult conditions.
The issue of the supply of Belarusian agricultural equipment and the use of financial mechanisms will be touched upon - they are needed in order to reduce the cost of cars for the final consumer.
Problems were discussed in the work of the Tyumen trading house “Belshina” and options to prevent losses.
important issues, since investment projects should clearly work and bring profit to the region.
It was talked about further deliveries of passenger and trucking of OJSC "MAZ", the development of the MAZ service center, which was established in Tyumen on the basis of OJSC "TPATP".
Conversation also touched upon the preparation of the trip of the working delegation of the region to the Republic of Belarus before the end of this year.
Another topic of the conversation was the completion of coordination and the signing of an agreement on trade, economic, scientific, technical and cultural co-operation between the Tyumen region and the Republic of Belarus.
Thus, the dynamics of relations promises to reach a new level.
These questions also applied to the regional center.
During the meeting with the head of the Tyumen city administration Alexander Moor, we were talking about the renovation of the Tyumen bus fleet.
Approximately 100 buses are already "breathing incense", because a new batch of cars from Belarus is required, which will work on gas, environmentally friendly fuel.
Another aspect: the Tyumen elevator plant cooperates with one of the leading manufacturers of Elevator products OJSC “Mogilevliftmash”, receiving components.
In my opinion, this activity could become more active, taking into account programs for the installation of new elevators in the regional center.
I will add that as part of the enlarged powers of the consul there was a meeting with the governor of the Kurghan region Alexei Kokorin, during which the issue of increasing trade and the supply of modern Belarusian equipment in the Urals was discussed.
At the end of September it is planned to meet with the Omsk governor.
The enlarged consular district consists of five subjects of the Russian Federation, but Tyumen can be called a kind of district headquarters.
The region is a landfill for testing of many promising projects, including the work of an honorary consul.
In general, such meetings are significant and are good in the fact that it allows you to directly and quickly solve many problems, responsive to their severity and developing mutually beneficial cooperation.
In the current conditions, it is extremely important not to destruse the reserve, continuing to work for the future.
