It is not known whether the actor accepted an invitation and whether he met with the Pope.
“American Ninja Warrior” awarded the first champion
A professional climber and assistant waiter Isaac Caldiero on Monday evening became the first winner of American Ninja Warrior, borrowing a prize of $ 1 million home.
On this sports show, season 7 of which has just ended, none of the participants have yet managed to go through all the stages of the track with obstacles.
In the end of the season, the two participants - Caldero and cameraman Jeff Britten, reached the final round.
The final task included climbing the rope with a length of 75 feet in 30 seconds.
Britten performed the task first and met at a predetermined time, becoming the first athlept in the history of "American Ninja Warrior", passed the greaking stage 4, but Caldiero coped with the task as much as three seconds faster, which made it a winner.
After the victory, inherited with an incredible work, Caldiero, who was astonished of winning a million-dol dollars, gave an interview to "E!News".
“To think about it is unbelievable, I’ve never earned and didn’t live on more than $10,000 per a year,” Iyzek told reporters E!
Suddenly, I never even imagined what it used to be ... the future is unknown.
Executive Producer Könt Weed met with the Hollywood Reporter journalists to talk about the ending and why Britten, who was the first track, will not receive a cash prize.
According to the rules, money is received by the fastest participant.
“If there’s more than one of those finishing players, the prize receives the fastest of them,” Wyd said.
Although the money - a wonderful reward and changes life, it still receives a lot of satisfaction.
I don't think he feels offended.
He’s happy with what he has done.
He received a ton of enthusiastic reviews from the fans.
He's a lovely man and a family man.
He is a hero for his children and a wife.
Jeff told me, "If I'm meant to lose to someone, I'm glad it's Isaac."
And I think that Isaac would feel the Same way if we switched their roles.
Amreika Ninja Warrior will return with eighth season, which will start filmed in the spring of 2016.
