Kadyrov's original complaint from the book "Molnaze to God" went to the Yuzhno-Sakhalinsk court.
Yuzhno-Sakhalinsk city court received the original appeal of the representative of the President of Chechnya Ramzan Kadyrov on the decision to “extremist material” of the book “Phobbage to God: its significance and place in Islam”, reports “Interfax” with reference to the Chairman of the city court Alexander Chukhray.
Now the court awaits possible objections to the participants of the process.
Chukhra refused to comment on the statements of some deputies of the state Duma of the Russian Federation about the need to check the city for possible cooperation with foreign special special services and ISIS.
“Like themselves comment on such stupidities,” he said.
On September 11, the Yuzhno-Sakhalinsk City Prosecutor's Office lodged an appeal against Judge Natali Perchenko's decision to recognize the book as “extremist material”.
The Yuzhno-Sakhalinsk prosecutor's office received an appeal on Friday evening.
There are nuances in the Prosecutor’s office believe that they asked the court to recognize as extremist only the opinion of the author of this book, and not verses from the Quran.
According to the Prosecutor’s office, the judge took the wrong decision”, – said Chukhray.
Recognition of the book “extremist material” was adopted on August 12, 2015
In particular, “extremist” quotes from the Quran – “We worship you and we pray to you for help”, “Do not appeal to anyone along with Allah”.
Kadyrov called who made a decision on the book “Shaitans and provocateurs”.
Deputies of the state Duma he called for bygulatory prohibiting judicial decisions regarding the texts of sacred scriptures.
“I am firmly convinced that the state Duma should adopt a law according to which it is prohibited to make in court decisions relating directly to the Qur’an and other Divine Writings,” Kadyrov wrote on Instagram.
Facebook Will Rescue Compliments Afforcing Immigrants and Refuge
Employees “Facebook” intends to remove posts and comments, which gives a negative assessment to migrants and refugees.
In addition, the social network will financially provide financial support to organizations that collect user complaints about illegal content.
To combat manifestations of xenophobic and racism in the network, the leadership of “Facebook” is going to work together with the Ministry of justice of Germany.
So, on the eve of the head of the Department Heiko Maas said that at the present time the Ministry of justice together with the specialists of the social network is engaged in the creation of a special group of moderators.
Its participants are obliged to monitor and remove incorrect comments to migrants and refugees.
According to Heiko Maas, it is assumed that the authors of intolerant posts will receive notifications indicating the reasons for deleting their recording.
To facilitate the rapid blocking of illegal content should also be organizations whose specialists are engaged in the collection of compensating complaints from users of the social network against offensive posts.
“Facebook management” intends to provide them with the necessary financial support.
The decision to delete posts containing negative statements against migrants and refugees, the leadership of the social network and the German justice ministry was made after xenophobic sentiments rose sharply.
One of the most obvious reasons for them was an unparalleled migratory crisis, which engulfed the countries of the European Union some time ago.
So, in Germany is already overcrowded today all points intended for the placement of refugees.
On the eve of the authorities of the country decided to temporarily settle migrants on the territory of the former Buchenwald concentration camp.
Forced Imigrators from the Middle East and Africa are placed in barracks, where prisoners and prisoners of war were detained under the Nazi regime.
There will be zones for relaxation in Moscow cemeteries.
In the near future at once, several metropolitan cemeteries will be equipped with specialized areas for relaxation and psychological recreation.
Among the first will be Butovo, Domodedovo, and Shcherbinsky Cemetery.
The first zone for psychological recreation has already appeared at the Troekurovsky cemetery in Moscow.
In the future, similar sites will appear in other areas of the city.
Artem Ekimov told about this portal m24.ru, who holds the position of head of the state budgetary institution "Ritual".
Relaxation zones will represent small landslital areas resemigating parks.
According to experts, in such “correxes”, visitors of cemeteries will be able to rest, be alone with themselves and restore psychological forces.
In the near future, zones for relaxation will be built in Domodedovsky, Butovo and Shcherbinsky cemeteries, and then in other districts of the capital.
According to the head of GBU "Ritual", if there is a need to expand the areas of the cerepod, the builders will try to preserve the existing forests to the maximum extent possible.
Green plantations will serve as a living fence, which will separate the recreation and areas allotted directly for burial sites.
Ritual GBU experts also expressed their intention to make a proposal to refuse hedgets at burial grounds.
New cemeteries can really become barrier-free.
In addition, GBU “Ritual” told about the readiness to engage in the installation of electronic terminals, with the help of which cemeteries visitors will be able to recognize GPS-coordinates and burial signs.
In June of this year in GBU "Ritual" was also proposed to adjust the cost of burial services, depending on the time of the year.
So, the chant of the tomb in the summer will cost a thousand rubles cheaper, a week in the winter, when the land is frozen.
It should not be noted that over the past year, the prices for all types of funeral services have risen in price by an average of 10 percent.
In the Yellnian forests after five days found lost mushroom growers.
The elderly man found himself alive, although he spent more than a hundred hours more often than a month without provisions.
To find grief mushroom managed thanks to the joint efforts of rescuers and volunteers.
Alexander Blynnikov, correspondent: "79-year-old pensioner from the Tambov region spent in the forest five days."
There's no meal or food.
Relgiments and volunteers were looking for him.
There were even cynologists with dogs, but there was no result.
To detect the man was able after a helicopter was connected to the exploratory work.
On that day Vitaly Alexandriovich as usual went to the forest for mushrooms and bakeries, but by the evening he did not come back.
Relatives immediately appealed for help, and the next day in search of the mushroom grower, rescuers and caring residents from a neighboring village - a total of about 30 people were raised in search of a mushroom.
For the fifth day they were contacted by a helicopter of a firefighting and rescue center.
Andrey Seletkov, the head of the search and rescue group of a detachment of a fire-rescue Center of the Smolensk region, said: "The helicopter was attracted, the man was found."
Left very far, completely somewhere else.
This was approximately 12 km from the place of the search.
He walked a huge distance at his age.
Miraculously survived.
Gribnik was taken to the Yellninsky central district hospital unconstitious, in an extremely serious condition.
Physicians diagnosed his pneumonia, as well as severe dehydration and hypothermia of the body.
As an elderly man was able to remain alive after five days spent in the afternoon, the doctors do not know at all.
Alina Nepsha, head of the therapeutic department of Yellninsky CRB: "Appointed an examination to the patient, treatment."
Inffusion therapy, antibacterial
Taking into account all its chronic diseases.
The condition of the patient in the in the morning has improved, remains heavy, but with positive dynamics.
Retier Vitaly Aleksandrovich every year comes to Smolenshchina from the Tambov region.
His grandson says that his grandparior previously went to collect mushroom mushrooms, but he had never delved into the timber.
Alexey Sppchenko, the grandson of the mushroom grower, shared: "The forest is not far from the road, himself in principle is not a local one."
Literally for a few years he came to visit, to visit his relatives.
So he went for mushroom mushrooms.
Apparently, went too far and got lost.
With the beginning of the mushroom season, people are regularly lost in all areas of the Smolensk region.
Only in the last a few days, there are five similar cases.
Rescuers reminiscances remind you that in the forest you need to go in bright clothes, with a small supply of merchandise, matches and a compass.
In addition, it is advisabilable to leave traces, so you can then go back.
Ambigned An-2 landed on a sack in a fraternal taiga.
Directly on the siege sat down in Siberia emergency An-2.
An emergency landing plane of the Krasnoyarsk airline "Yenisei" made 68 kilometers from Bratsk.
There are no dead or injured, but the plane itself received significant damage upon landing.
AN-2 made an official flight.
On board there were three crew members - the commander, the co-pilot and the flight mechanic, reports "Interfax".
The emergency aircraft made a flight along the route Zheleznogorsk-Ilimsky - Achinsk, where the airline is based.
Crew of the aircraft has already been delivered to Bratsk.
Fraternal transport Prosecutor’s office after an emergency landing of An-2 began an inspection of compliance with the legislation on flight safety.
Investigative group of the East Siberian transport prosecutor's office went to the scene of the incident.
In September 2010, the crew of the Tu-154 landed its plane with passengers because of a technical malfunction on an abandoned taiga airfield in Komi.
On the liner refused the engines and on-board electronics, but the crew did the impossible.
On board the aircraft there were 10 crew members and 72 passengers.
No one was injured in an emergency landing.
The Nobel Laureate: Globalization
The processes of globalization should have helped to reduce inequalities in the world.
In fact, the situation looks different, the difference in the income of the population in the developing economies, on the contrary, is growing.
Eric Muskin.
In order to fix this, it is Necessary to increase the level of education of low-skilled workers, said the chief researcher, chief researcher of the International Laboratory for Analysis and Choice of Judicial Solutions of HSE, Nobel laureate in economics Eric Maskin.
In the last twenty years, the world has experienced an unpreceinable growth of global markets.
The trade borders between countries have become more and more open.
Proponents of globalization predicted great benefits for developing economies.
“And these predictions have largely come true,” Maskin emphasizes.
So, for example, China and India received a significant growth of GDP per capita.
It’s not all so raking.
Globalization was expected to reduce the glourage between “possessessessessessessesses” and “poor” in poor countries, which is manifested in a large inequity of income, or rather – wages.
But in fact this inequality has only risen, says Eric Maskin in his article “Why Global Markets Didn’t Reduce Indigenated Ineligible in Developing Economies”, Published in The World’s Bank Economic Review, which was translated and quoted by HSE.
In conjunction with an economist at Harvard University Professor Michael Kremer, Eric Maskin has developed an alternative theory that demonstrates why income margins in poor countries increase as globalization grows.
In the new global market there are specific processes taking place.
To demonstrate them, Maskin allocates the four levels of qualification of specialists - A and B for rich countries, C and D - for the poor.
After globalization, D specialists from poor countries do not have enough qualifications to cooperate with specialists A and B from rich countries.
And, if C workers from poor countries are growing due to cooperation with employees B of the rich, D workers do not feel growth or their salaries are falling at all.
The final effect is such that the internationalization of production will contribute to an increase in the wage gap between the two categories of specialists in poor countries and consequently an increase in inequalities.
Kremer and E. Maskin proposed an amazingly beautiful model, an alternative to Rycardian theory of comparative advantages.
It allows you to explain why globalization led to inequalities in income, says Fuad Aleskerov, an ordinary professor, the head of the International Laboratory for Analysis and Solutions, Head of Mathematics.
And as every powerful theory, I am sure it will lead to a spike of empiracious work in this area.
The solution, according to Erick Muskin, lies in raising the level of education of low-skilled workers.
However, the workers themselves, as the scientist notes, do not have the funds for this, and it is undesuitable for companies to pay for their training.
In such a situation, governments, international agencies, NGOs and private funds can play a significant role, Maskin said.
The scientist notes that the developed theory in any case does not in any way call to stop the process of globalization, which has brought and bears its fruit in the form of GDP growth of countries.
Derbent: a living connection of times.
Derbent - one of the most ancient cities of Russia - in September celebrates its 2000-year anniversary.
The festive events program includes the festival of national cultures of the peoples of Dagestan and the fair in the style of past times, an exhibition of derbant carpets and the Day of open temples, the historical and musical show “2000 in two o’clock in two hours” and an excursion to the reconstructed museum of Peter I.
Medieval stones of Naryn-Kala Fortress, ancient Arabic inscriptions on the walls, narrow streets and palace ordains - it's as if it had descended from "Thous and Thousand and One Nights".
Derbent is the only city in Russia, preserved in its place since ancient times.
Although it was claimed by the Roman Empire, Byzantium, Khazarian Khaganate and the Golden Horde.
The age of oriental strays, which are growing in the yard of the derbant Juma Mosque, is equal to several centenies.
These powerful plants are protected by the All-Misonic program "Christmas Trees - Survival Monuments".
The shadow of sprawling kroons save pilgrims and tourists during the summer heat.
The visitor of the mosque will pour fragrant tea and be cursed with Dagestani delicacies - honey figs, persimmons, mushmula, frosts-sang, ayran and sweets.
In Derbubta from time immemorial used large samovars to at one time to water the tea of numerous guests.
Inscribish over the entrance to the Juma Mosque says that the building was built in the age of hijra.
That is, in 733 according to the Gregorian Calendar.
This is the oldest mosque in Russia.
The interior amazes the scope and paciful: the arcade of domes and veneers are relied on square columns and are illuminated by genuine rays from tiny windows.
Maintenance and brewing of pigeons is a traditional fascination of Derbent residents.
Owners of poultry poultries put pigeon coats in yards, under the trees, in the attics.
Excavating spectacle - a floach of white pigeons into the sky, similar to the flares of festive fireworks.
For the purpose of defense from the brigadier, the ancient Persians blocked the Caspian Gate with a double stone wall.
Leaving for 500 meters into the sea, this building was locked by Derbent Harbor.
In 2003 Derbent's Fortress Walls Were Included in the UNESCO World Heritage List as the most well-preserved Monument of Ancient Persian Forteaching.
Carpets in Derbent thawed back in the 5th century, and to this day the technology of this unique reifiments has survived almost unchanged.
On one of the streets adjacent to the urban market, carpets are sold for every taste - wool pillars, cotton or felt of all colors and hues, with pile and without it, with difficult ornaments and bizardrical kayama.
The construction of the city began with Magals - blocks with one-story stone buildings.
For many years, the Magals have not changed much.
Only satellite sauces, air conditioners on the walls and outdoor lanmonaries remind you that you are not in a medieval, but in a modern city.
In the old part of the city preserved the details of the plumb, built by the Persians about a thousand years.
To this day came the ancient sources in which the locals are still gaining water.
Many derbants prefer ordinary water from faucets water from proven historical fountains.
In Derbent there was one of the centers of the potter's cushions.
Irrigation vases, meals, pitchfortunes, cups were valued in the whole of the Caucasus.
The hands of the potters are now producing wonderful ceramic products of both practical and souvenir terms.
In the days of holidays and festivals, crowds of spectators are gathered under a stretched rope at which the students of the Republican Circus Art school perform.
The history of an astonishing and risky mastery dates back several centuries.
A new trend - one more and more often can be seen girls.
In the premises of the former Magnitude Bath today there is a museum "Culture and everyday life of Ancient Derbent".
Previously, unmarried girls and fiancées were washed here, accompanied by girlfriends, and now anyone can see a vintage and dome hall, a hot and cold swimming pool that have gone into the past of swimming supplies.
In most Derbubta’s houses have hot water, but the buns and plumber these days are as popular as in the old days.
About the benefits of warming the body by ferry is written in ancient books.
After the bang, the blood improves, the muscles lose fatigue, the body acquires flexibility and ease.
In the festival "Commonwealth", which takes place on the territory of Naryn-Cala fortress, are attended by ethnic courtyards of many districts of Dagestan.
The participants in national costumes dance, play folk melodies, perform songs of the peoples of the Caucasus and treat visitors with tasty domestic cheese.
Kyrkhlyar is a burial place of forty martyrs, who laid down their heads for Islam.
This is one of the most revered complexes for Muslims of the North-Caucasus.
Jenny sarcophagus are carved from whole stone blocks and oriented, as is customary among the Arabs, along the axis of the west-east.
Gevril and Albert Jakubov are tonsure and shave customers in a small salon near the Upper Bazaar.
Hairdresser in this place has been located for many years.
Acceptances of the circulatory receptacles are transmitted from generation to generation.
At the same time, the Yakubov brothers can make not only a traditional, but also the most modern hairstyle.
On one of the streets of the Old Town there is a house in which there lived a Decebrist writer Alexander Bestuzhev-Marlinsky.
Having studied the Turkic language and collecting ethnographic material, he described Dyerbent of the first third of the XIX century with its ancient monuments, the life and everyday life of the citizens.
Chaikhana is a traditional club of the East, which serves only tea and homemade pastries.
Men come to quench thirst here, communicate with your friends and solve some working problems.
As in previous times, women are not recommended to overcome the threshold of Tekhanov.
Derbent dance ensemble "Caspium" was created three years ago, but has already managed to take part in events of the republican and Russian levels.
The soloists of the ensemble rehearse every day, destitulitizing the traditional Avar, Darginsky, tat, Armenian dances.
With the onset of the evening, when the noise subslides and street lanmonaries are lit, the locals scatter on benches near houses with protruding terraces.
As a rule, derbants discuss domestic issues.
But on the eve of the anniversary, they increasingly commemorate episodes of the unique history of their city, inflaring the fate of the entire Black Sea-Caspian region.
In Domodedovo there was a business “game for the airport”.
In the capital they are experiencing a new form of training.
Four hundred students have tried themselves as airport employees.
To do this in Domodedova mounted models of three harbies.
The young people not only inspected and registered the passengers, but also served the planes.
All this - in the form of a business game, but in terms of complexity it did not concede of reality.
Late flights, at once two passengers with fractures on board, the ladder was lost somewhere on the way to the plane.
For a real airport - hell.
For the one who has settled in Domodedova hangar - a standard set of tasks that beginners will have to solve.
In the same hangar accommodated three large airports from around the country around the world.
Today they employ four hundred students from the capital's colleges and universities.
Unprecedented chance to find out everything about the inner world of the air harbour.
Registration of passengers, maintenance of airplanes, the turnover of luggage - they were trusted even by buses on the flight field, ladders and passenger inspection.
Passengers are all problematic.
One is dishlied with the documents, the other was late for the flight, the third filled the bag with suspicious items.
And you need to deal with all of this, as in a life - in a minimum period of time.
For each of these completed tasks, a certain amount is accrued a certain amount, a virtual money, as if the airline had paid the corresponding amounts for the maintenance of the flight.
“For the failure to fulfill the relevant tasks, a pen leotid is collected from them,” Dmitry Khilko, a financial Analypalitologist of the game, explains in an interview with Vesti-Mosquica.
Opportunities are closely monitored by officials from the Ministry of Education.
For them, this exam - an attempt to try a new form of training.
She has already found a place at the secondary vocational education.
“Six inter-regional centers of competence will be formed, which will, in fact, become new models for the activities of modern colleges with a modern management system, with highly qualified personnel, with modern equipment,” said Natalia Zolotareva, director of the department of state policy in the field of training and additional professional education of the Ministry of Education and Science of Russia.
But for students - not up to global plans.
After the three-dreath of such a workout, it seems they will need a day off.
But the grades for this exam had quite a material expression.
Recent smart glasses, the best I’ve ever seen!
“I received them for the fact that in a timely manner responded to the claim to our airport on Instagram”, – is satisfied the participant of the game, the PR-manager of “Airport Frankfurt” Sergey Shuvalov.
The best judges, as they say, were taken on a pencil in order to invoice to their studies at the end of their studies to work.
The U.S. Embassy deplores the closure of the American center in Moscow.
The American Embassy in Russia deplored in connection with the cloumination in force at the Library of Foreign Literature of an American center.
The center worked in Moscow for more than 22 years.
The US Embassy in Moscow deeply deplories about the unilateral decision of the Russian government to clapprote the American center of the U.S. Embassaber of the U.I. Rudino All-Russian State Library in Moscow.
“Specreary-negotiable steps taken by Russia have called into question Russia’s commitment to relations between the Russian and American peoples, which have not been interrupted even during the Cold War and at other difficult moments in the long history of relations between our countries,” U.S. Ambassador John Tefft said in a statement to Interfax.
The American Center created deep and strong ties between people and the culture of Russia and the United States.
It was the center of American culture, history and literature in the Russian capital, and also served as a place of meetings with numerous American evisvisimed figures, among whom were astronauts, artists, athletes, scientists, politicians and writers.
“Last last year the American center conducted more than 400 cultural and educational events and received more than 50 thousand Russian visitors”, – said the diplomat.
TEft recalled that about a year ago it was decided to clapple another joint Russian-American project - the program of educational interchange FLEX (Future Leaders Exchange Program).
The Green Trial was quick to kill.
A typical situation: the four officials are in front of the table of Judge Svantaire Kumar, echoing his claims to the work done.
Judgment is completely dissatisfied with the quality of your work.
We didn’t give you a 110-page order, so that you would make you laugh at it, says Kumar.
If there will be at least one more brick, we are ordered to demolish all the existing buildings.
Kumar heads the National Green Jurisprudence, a judicial authority established in 2010 to halt the rapid environmental pollution accompanying rapid economic growth in recent decades.
During this time, the Tribunal managed to consider more than 10 thousand claims related to air pollution, garbage collection, geological developments, toxic waste and the construction of dams.
In two out of three cases, the court makes a decision to stop construction leading to pollution.
Bets are incredibly high: in the incomplete 60 years that have elapsed since the declared independence of enhanced industrial development, India has turned from a country of virgin jungle into one of the most obsessed and polluted countries in the world.
Participating problem is especially acute in large megacities, where the development of the infrastructure does not support rapid urbanization: the cities are covered with dense smog, the rivers are filled with pesticides and waste of enterprises and households, and a few remaining residential areas are cut down for construction with new residential areas.
Despite the formal support of the green movement on the part of the state, NZT is regularly criticized by the government of Narendra Modi, as it often becomes the main reason for the cancellation of the largest investment projects.
So, in may of this year the Minister of environment called the court’s decisions “extremist” and “impossible”.
Occasionally it is really impossible to comply with the period set by the court, confirms legal lawyer for environmental cases Raj Panjvani.
However, impracticable deadlines have a positive side: at the very least, they are forcing responsible persons to move.
“His main goal is to shatter this system”, – the lawyer adds.
The Green Tribunal has repeatedly abolished large construction sites: the termination of the airport, the power plant and hundreds of smaller installations on account.
At the same time, people also try not to forget: for example, during the discussion of the fate of a pharmaceutical company in the state of Telagnan, polluting the local fluoride river.
We can close your factory, but we are also responsible for the economic aftermath.
“People will lose their jobs,” Kumar commented.
However, such explanations do not always find an understanding among ordinary people, whose lives can be changed thanks to one stroke of the judicial feather.
So, in April, the Tribunal decided to prohibit all vehicles older than 10 years of entry into the capital, which aroused popular indignation.
“Desptually falling popularity and slurry of criticism, Svantánter Kumar refused to repeal this decision.
Instead, he commissioned statistics on entering and departing vehicles, and also made an offer to purchase 10 thousand additional buses, having previously recognized in the factories whether they are able to fulfill such an order.
As cases began to fall into the attention of the court began to get such sources of pollution as landfills, the quality of the fuel and even road accidents, popular wretched began to gradually subside.
But the most sorcerable topic of the principal judge was the program to clean the Ganges River, with a pump announced by Prime Minister Narendra Modi last year.
When it comes to the Ganges - a sacred river for Hindus, the judge often ceases to restrain his emotions and switches to screaming.
Do you know what "hostile" means?
Someone poured water from the Gang on a statue of God, and there were faeces in it - the judge is ardent.
You keep contaminating the river, because you are thinking: Gang is a Gang, he will take all our sins.
It’s the river that we worship and see what you’re dealing with it every day.
Clipping Gang is the most ambitious and cost-vesting environmental project announcing the new government.
Currently, the number of fecal bacterical bacteria in this river exceeds the norm by more than 120 times.
Every year, from 1.5 to 3 out of 700 million bathing Hindus die from infectious diseases.
In February, Narendra Modi even donated to the Gang Gang Saving Fund the proceeds from the sale of his suit, in which he encountered with Barack Obama and another 455 items from his personal collection.
Ecologists immediately accused the premiere of populism: the costume was bought for 700 thousand dollars, while at least $ 8 billion is required for cleaning the river.
Proponents of the Green Tribunal agree that India still has a long way to go before it can call itself a developed country, but they do not believe that the cost of progress should be ecology.
“In a developing country, talks about the environment are often perceived as an impermissible luxury,” says Malika Bhanot, an activist at Zov Gang.
And the court is trying to find a middle ground between ecology and development.”
The man poured the blood of Dali paintings at an exhibition in Riga.
A visitor of the exhibition of the Latvian Union of Artists in Riga shattered the windows in a museum and spoiled Salvador Dali's "Appearance of an an angel".
Now in the museum there is an exhibition of works by El Salvador Dali and Pablo Picasso.
A man born in 1985 entered the sculpture hall at 14:20.
Immediately behaved inadequately: he spoiled the sculpture, smashed the windows.
Then he began to move around the premises and squeezed several works of the permanent exhibition with blood.
Among them is a portrait of Poruk the brush of Myervalddis Polis.
According to the President of the Latvian Union of Artists Igor Dobychin, who refers “Interfax”, were also spoiled showcases.
At the scene there are police and art experts.
The latter determine the amount of the damage and the damage.
A criminal case of hooliganism was initiated against the man.
In the Latvian Confederation of Artists from August 4 to September 27 is an exhibition of works by Picasso and Dali, which presents more than 200 original works of artists.
