The Volgograd Governor and akim of the West-Kazakh region signed an agreement on cooperation.
On September 16, the XII Inter-Regional Inter-Regional Cooperation Forum between Russia and Kazakhstan was opened in Sochi.
The key topic is interaction in the agro-industry complex and ensuring food security.
The regional forum is also attended by the Governor of the Volgograd region Andrey Bocharov.
It should be noted that Kazakhstan is one of the strategic partners of our region.
Economic co-operation is increasing every year, as well as cultural ties are strengthened.
On September 16, Andrei Bocharov and the akim of the West-Kazakhstan Oblast Nurlan Nogayev signed an agreement on cooperation.
The document will make it possible to create favorable conditions for the mutual supply of goods, as well as to increase the interaction of industrial enterprises.
The Russian-Belaro-Belarusian “Shield of the Union-2015” has ended.
In the west of the country ended joint Russian-Belarusian exercises “Shield of the Union-2015”, according to “Rossoy 24”.
The manoeuvres took place at training grounds in the Leningrad, Pskov and Kaliningrad regions, as well as in the Baltic Sea.
Participated more than eight thousand servicemen and about four hundred pieces of equipment.
On the last day of the exercise, Baltflot ships worked out an artillery attack on naval and coastal targets, as well as repelling an airborne anti-environment.
Where can I leave a review about the bailiff in Murmansk?
In the Department of the Federal bailiff service in the Murmansk region it was said that in order to improve the work on the protection of the rights and legitimate interests of citizens and organizations in the department there is a book of reviews and proposals.
In it, citizens can leave a record about the quality of work of bailiff bailiffs-executors and other government officials, information on job deficiencies, as well as to express their proposals and wishes.
In the management of a copy of the book of recognizions and proposals is located in the central hall, in a special pocket in a visible and affordable place at the checkpoint into the building.
In the structural departments of management, the book is located in the Chancellery.
Taking into account the nature of the withdrawal or offer, if necessary, his initiator is sent a written response.
Xi Jinping Calls for Making Economies More Accelerated for Peace
The economy should become more open for the whole of the world to spur its growth, as President Xi Jinping said in an appeal to a group that faces the task of leading the reforms.
“China should concentrate on attracting foreign investors and experts and developing a policy of openness,” he said, appealing to the participants of the 16-th meeting of the Committee of the Central Leading Group for the Comprehensive Deployment of the reforms.
According to him, the expansion of the openness and deepening of the reforms will give the economy a new impetus and a vital force and will provide a new space for economic development.
The lead group adopted a number of directive directives, including the implementation of the regulation of investor access to the market, changing the rules of border control, encouraging state-owned enterprises (SOE), attracting private capital and revising the resident registration system.
According to the statement, will be compiled a list of sectors of the economy and production inaccessible for investment will be compiled.
The system will gradually dedicate through test programs.
This is an important step, since it will provide the market for a more significant role in the distribution of resources, ensuring legality in the business sphere and increasing openness, as stated in a statement.
The government will also weaken control over the powers provided to their companies, thereby guaranteeing that the companies themselves will conduct their own business.
The statement also said that China will allow the border regions to develop new models of transboundary economic co-operation and new mechanisms to strengthen local growth.
Even more spheres will be available for private investors in order to increase the openness of state-controlled sectors of the economy.
“The government won’t change its policy against foreign investors and will defend the legitimate interests of foreign-financial companies, as well as provide them with better conditions,” the statement said in a statement.
Additionally, the procedure for applying for a permanent residency permit for foreigners, or “Green-card”, will be facilitated by optimizing requirements and simplifying the filing process itself.
The meeting also discussed ensuring the rights of lawyers and the issues of training of professional judges and procuratorial officers.
According to an official report issued after the meeting, it was also attended by Prime Minister Li Keqiang and ministers Liu Yongshan and Zhang Gaoli.
